#
# prima-materia — Kabbalah: Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, with
# Histaklut Penimit to Part 1
#
# The harvest of one work of the corpus of pmt:Kabbalah, kept apart from
# traditions/kabbalah.ttl, which declares the tradition and the work
# (pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot); the edition read, the two Hebrew
# witnesses, the translations and the counts of the harvest stand as notes on
# the work there. Two units are read: the Introduction, whose nodes follow the
# author's sections 1 to 156 (Hebrew letters alef to qof-nun-vav, 71 absent
# from his numbering), each at the section that carries it; then Histaklut
# Penimit to Part 1, chapters 1 to 10, cited by chapter and by the paragraphs
# of the Sefaria segmentation.
#
# The Petiḥa le-Ḥokhmat ha-Qabbala and the Haqdama le-Sefer ha-Zohar by the
# same author are harvested in traditions/kabbalah-petiha.ttl and
# traditions/kabbalah-haqdama-zohar.ttl. The same assertion by the same author
# is not entered twice: every record of this harvest was compared with the
# nodes of those files, and where a node there carries the claim no node is
# written here (the mapping is kept with the harvest note); links into such
# claims point at those nodes. A node stands here when this work carries a
# claim no earlier node carries, or when it states a claim in a different
# form; such a node carries a note beginning "Differs from" that names the
# earlier node and the difference.
#
# Harvested under prima-materia#924 with two independent extraction passes
# over the Hebrew, reconciled by offset and word overlap, then integrated by a
# reader of the whole text. Identifiers are pmc:KabbalahAshlag or
# pmp:KabbalahAshlag plus the Hebrew term in ASCII transliteration. Signs of
# success, conditions of failure and capacities carry a note beginning
# "Counted as".
#


#
# §1
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagShelloYahmitz a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "The fear of going sour through Kabbalah"@en, "Furcht, durch Kabbala zu verderben"@de ;
    skos:definition "The third objection: cases occurred where people strayed from the Torah because of Kabbalah, so why endanger oneself; the author answers in §37 that the danger has two specific causes."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:KabbalahAshlagEsekBeHokhmatHaQabbala ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: שלא יחמיץ (shelo yachmitz)."@en ;
    skos:note "The author answers at §37 that the straying which did happen had two causes, entered as pmc:KabbalahAshlagGiluyDevarimAsurim and pmc:KabbalahAshlagHoraotGashmiyot."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§1 (א), 37 (לז), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagBneiToraShebeDori a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against the Torah scholars of his generation who leave the hidden"@en, "Gegen die Toragelehrten seiner Generation"@de ;
    skos:definition "The scholars of his generation are reported to drop the study of the hidden and advise a page of Gemara instead; the author answers at length that after the time limit they must turn to Kabbalah and that the whole people needs it."@en ;
    skos:note "A dispute entered as a concept: the opposing view is reported by the author and not read in a work of its own."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§1 (א), 36 (לו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §3
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagKiyyumHaToraTaamHaHayyim a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Keeping Torah yields the taste of life"@en, "Halten der Tora ergibt Lebensgeschmack"@de ;
    skos:definition "Keeping Torah and commandments properly is said to give the taste of true life and the seeing that God is good."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:KabbalahAshlagKiyyumHaToraKeHilkhata ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:KabbalahAshlagTaamHaHayyim ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §3 (ג), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagTaamHaHayyim a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Tasting the taste of life; seeing that the Lord is good"@en, "Geschmack des Lebens kosten; sehen, dass Gott gut ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Those who keep Torah and commandments properly are said to taste the real flavour of life and to see and testify from experience that God is good, i.e. that creation was made to benefit the creatures."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: טעם החיים / טעמו וראו כי טוב ה׳ (taam ha-chayim; taamu u-reu ki tov H)."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §3 (ג), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmp:KabbalahAshlagKiyyumHaToraKeHilkhata a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Keeping Torah and commandments according to their law"@en, "Tora und Gebote nach der Halacha halten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Whoever has not yet had a taste of the good life has no other counsel than to go and keep Torah and commandments according to their law."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: קיום התורה והמצות כהלכתם (kiyyum ha-Torah ve-ha-mitzvot ke-hilkhatam)."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:KabbalahAshlagTaryagMitzvotBeMaase (Haqdama, §44): the Haqdama sets keeping the commandments in deed as the first rung of a ladder that builds the partzuf of nefesh; here it is the only counsel for anyone still without a taste of the life the verse promises."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §3 (ג), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagHayyimBliToraQashimMiMavet a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Life without Torah harder than death"@en, "Leben ohne Tora schwerer als der Tod"@de ;
    skos:definition "Until the Torah was given, the text says, we had nothing but death and evil: the sages count the wicked as dead while alive because the pains of sustaining life far outweigh its small pleasure; a life lacking Torah and commandments pleases neither its owner nor anyone through his children, whose lives are as hard."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: רשעים בחייהם נקראים מתים (reshaim be-hayyeihem niqraim metim)."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that does not come about or is lost, and its cause. It names how pmc:KabbalahAshlagTaamHaHayyim fails or is lost."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:KabbalahAshlagMetimBeHayeihem (Petiha, §57): there the wicked are dead for a life wholly for themselves; here the saying is read of pain outweighing pleasure in a life without Torah, which reaches even to one's children."@en ;
    skos:note "Written by the integrator from the reading of §3; the first pass held it only inside the capacity pmc:KabbalahAshlagTaamHaHayyim."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §3 (ג), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §4
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagBehiraLeInyanHaHizzuq a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Choice applies only to strengthening oneself"@en, "Wahl nur in der Stärkung"@de ;
    skos:definition "God himself places man's hand on the good lot by giving him a glimpse of peace beyond a life of suffering, so he flees toward it; man's choice concerns only strengthening himself until purified."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: בחירה (bechirah)."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:KabbalahAshlagShneiDerakhimBehira (Haqdama, §16): there choice lies between the path of Torah and the path of suffering; here God Himself sets the hand on the good lot by a glimpse of peace, and choice lies only in strengthening oneself until the body is purified."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §4 (ד), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmp:KabbalahAshlagHitHazzequtBeDerekhHaTov a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Strengthening oneself on the good path by every device"@en, "Wahl als Selbststärkung auf dem guten Weg"@de ;
    skos:definition "Before purification is complete, free choice consists in strengthening oneself in the good way by every means and device one can find, doing all within one's power until the work of purifying is finished, so as not to collapse midway."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: בחירה … לענין החיזוק (bechirah le-inyan ha-chizzuk)."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:KabbalahAshlagKolHaAmtzaimLishma (Haqdama, §31): there a warning that every fitting means must be used to come to lishma; here the strengthening is the whole of free choice before the body is purified."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §4 (ד), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagZikkukhHaGuf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The purified body, with no will to receive for oneself"@en, "Geläuterter Körper (kein Wille, für sich zu empfangen)"@de ;
    skos:definition "A state reached by long labour in which the body no longer holds any desire to receive pleasure for itself; it is the condition for keeping Torah lishmah."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: זכוך הגוף (zikkukh ha-guf)."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:KabbalahAshlagHizdakkekhutHaGuf (Petiha, §10): there the body is purified by Torah done with bestowing intent and becomes fit for the abundance; here it is reached by the ascetic way of the Mishna and is the condition for lishma."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§4 (ד), 6 (ו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagShelloYippolBeEmtzaHaDerekh a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Lest one fall under the load midway"@en, "Nicht auf halbem Weg fallen"@de ;
    skos:definition "One must do all in one's power until the purification is complete, lest one fall under the load in the middle of the way."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:KabbalahAshlagHitHazzequtBeDerekhHaTov, pmp:KabbalahAshlagDarkahShelTora ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §4 (ד), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §5
#

pmp:KabbalahAshlagDarkahShelTora a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "The way of Torah: training oneself to refuse all pleasure (the first device)"@en, "Weg der Tora: asketische Gewöhnung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: (1) train oneself to accept nothing for self-gratification, not even in permitted and necessary bodily needs such as food, drink and sleep; (2) remove oneself from every pleasure that accompanies even the necessary supply of life, living literally a life of sorrow while toiling in Torah (bread with salt, measured water, sleeping on the ground); (3) once habituated and no will for self-pleasure remains, engage Torah and commandments likewise only to give contentment to the Maker."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: דרכה של תורה; התחבולה הראשונה (darkah shel Torah; ha-tachbulah ha-rishonah)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§5 (ה), 6 (ו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §6
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagLishmaPresupposesZikkukhHaGuf a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Lishma not without great labour in purifying the body"@en, "Läuterung vor lischma"@de ;
    skos:definition "Keeping Torah under its strict condition of bestowal is impossible except by great labour in purifying the body."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:KabbalahAshlagHaluqaGimelLishma ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:KabbalahAshlagZikkukhHaGuf ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Without great labour in purifying the body one cannot come to keep Torah and commandments for the Maker alone." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §6 (ו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagDarkahShelToraZikkukhHaGuf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "The way of Torah yields the purified body"@en, "Asketische Gewöhnung ergibt Läuterung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Habituating oneself to refuse all self-pleasure is said to bring the state where no will to receive remains in the body."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:KabbalahAshlagDarkahShelTora ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:KabbalahAshlagZikkukhHaGuf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §6 (ו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagLishmaPresupposesHergel a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "First the habit of refusing pleasure, then study for the Maker"@en, "Erst Gewöhnung, dann gebendes Lernen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Only after one has become habituated to refusing self-pleasure can one from then on engage Torah for the Maker."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:KabbalahAshlagHaluqaGimelLishma ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:KabbalahAshlagDarkahShelTora ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    skos:note "The text sets the order and says nothing of what follows from skipping it; hence prescribed order."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §6 (ו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagEinRatzonLeQabbelBaGuf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sign: no will to receive left in the body"@en, "Kein Empfangswille mehr im Körper"@de ;
    skos:definition "The mark that habituation succeeded: the body no longer holds any desire to receive pleasure for itself."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: the text announces it as the mark of completion."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §6 (ו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagDarkahShelToraLishma a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "The way of Torah leads to lishma"@en, "Asketischer Weg führt zu lischma"@de ;
    skos:definition "After habituation one is able to engage Torah and commandments only for the Maker's contentment."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:KabbalahAshlagDarkahShelTora ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:KabbalahAshlagHaluqaGimelLishma ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §6 (ו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagHayyeiOsher a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The happy life: the whole world worthwhile for him"@en, "Glückliches Leben in dieser und der kommenden Welt"@de ;
    skos:definition "One who reaches lishmah is said to taste a life full of good and delight without any admixture of pain, to see in himself the purpose of creation, to rejoice in his years and to find the whole world worthwhile for him, even in this world."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: חיי אושר / אשריך בעוה\"ז (chayei osher; ashrekha ba-olam ha-zeh)."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§6 (ו), 9 (ט), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagLishmaHayyeiOsher a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Torah for its own sake yields the happy life"@en, "Lischma ergibt glückliches Leben"@de ;
    skos:definition "On reaching lishmah one tastes the happy life without any pain."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:KabbalahAshlagTorahUMitzvotAlMenatLeHashpia ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:KabbalahAshlagHayyeiOsher ;
    skos:note "The practice is the Petiha's Torah and commandments done to give contentment to the Maker, which the text here calls lishma."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §6 (ו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagLishmaRazeiTora a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Torah for its own sake yields the secrets of Torah"@en, "Lischma ergibt Geheimnisse der Tora"@de ;
    skos:definition "Torah lishmah is said to earn many things, among them the disclosure of Torah's secrets."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:KabbalahAshlagTorahUMitzvotAlMenatLeHashpia ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:KabbalahAshlagRazeiTora ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §6 (ו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagRazeiTora a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The secrets of Torah revealed: his soul teaches him"@en, "Offenbarung der Geheimnisse der Tora"@de ;
    skos:definition "Through Torah lishmah the secrets of Torah are said to be revealed to the person like a strengthening spring; the author tells the objector that one who already practises lishmah needs no Kabbalah books, since his own soul teaches him."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: רזי תורה; נשמת אדם תלמדנו (razei Torah; nishmat adam telamdenu)."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "The first passage is R. Meir in Avot 6 quoted as proof; the second is the author applying it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§6 (ו), 25 (כה), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §7
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagShneiHaTzedadimShebaMatbea a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The coin of Torah and its two sides"@en, "Zwei Seiten der Münze"@de ;
    skos:definition "Torah has two sides: the way of Torah, a long preparation of purifying the body with study necessarily shelo lishmah and a life of sorrow; and, after completion, a life of delight and peace that was the purpose of creation."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: שני הצדדים שבמטבע (shnei ha-tzedadim she-ba-matbea)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §7 (ז), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagMiShelloLishmaLeHayyeiOsher a pm:Sequencing ;
    rdfs:label "From the way of Torah to the happy life"@en, "Von schelo lischma zum glücklichen Leben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Three stages in the order the source gives them: the way of Torah, study not yet for its own sake with a life of sorrow that purifies the body; the purified body, able to engage for the Maker alone; and the happy life, in which the whole world is worthwhile."@en ;
    rdf:_1 pmp:KabbalahAshlagDarkahShelTora ;
    rdf:_2 pmc:KabbalahAshlagZikkukhHaGuf ;
    rdf:_3 pmc:KabbalahAshlagHaluqaGimelLishma ;
    rdf:_4 pmc:KabbalahAshlagHayyeiOsher ;
    pm:seriesStatement "The source sets the order: the way of Torah, with its life of sorrow and study not yet for its own sake, purifies the body; the purified body can engage for the Maker alone; that engagement brings the happy life. The first stage is one side of the coin and the last its other side, and the middle stands between them." ;
    skos:note "The source names a consequence of skipping the purification, entered as pmc:KabbalahAshlagLishmaPresupposesZikkukhHaGuf."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §7 (ז), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §8
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagToraVeShearHokhmot a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Torah unlike the other wisdoms"@en, "Tora unterscheidet sich von anderen Weisheiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Other wisdoms do not better life and need only toil; Torah aims to make man fit to receive the divine good and therefore requires purifying the body."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §8 (ח), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §9
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagDarkahShelToraHayyeiOsher a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Completing the way of Torah yields happiness in this world"@en, "Vollendung des Wegs ergibt Glück in dieser Welt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The happy life of this world is prepared solely for the one who finished the way of Torah."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:KabbalahAshlagDarkahShelTora ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:KabbalahAshlagHayyeiOsher ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §9 (ט), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §10
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagOrHaGanuz a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The hidden light: this world after the body is purified"@en, "Das verborgene Licht"@de ;
    skos:definition "The light of the first day included the life of this world in full delight, but was hidden for the righteous for the future, read as the time after their body is purified in the way of Torah, when they are worthy of it even in this world."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: גנזו לצדיקים לעתיד לבא."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §10 (י), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §11
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagHakalatHakhmeiHaTalmud a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The Talmudic sages eased the way of the Mishna"@en, "Mischnaischer gegen talmudischer Weg"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Talmudic sages are said to have eased the way of Torah compared with the Mishnaic sages by replacing ascetic practice with the Light in Torah."@en ;
    skos:note "Entered as a concept: the text contrasts two rulings it reads, the Mishna of Avot and the Talmud's saying about study shelo lishma; it holds the second an easing of the first and does not set them in dispute."@en ;
    skos:note "Contrast of two traditions, not polemic."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §11 (יא), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmp:KabbalahAshlagShelloLishmaBeEmuna a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Studying even shelo lishma, from faith"@en, "Torastudium auch schelo lischma (mit Glauben)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Engage in Torah and commandments even when not yet lishmah, i.e. believing in God, Torah and reward and punishment and studying because God commanded it, while still mixing in self-benefit; the Light in the Torah is said to bring one back to the good and to lishmah, in place of the ascetic way."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: שלא לשמה (shelo lishmah)."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:KabbalahAshlagShelloLishma (Haqdama, §31): the Haqdama prescribes engagement not for its own sake without condition; here it is defined as study from faith in God, Torah and reward and punishment, because He commanded it, and it is bound to that faith as its condition."@en ;
    skos:note "Presented as an innovation of the Talmudic sages that eases the Mishnaic way."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§11 (יא), 12 (יב), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagShelloLishmaBeEmunaLishma a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Not for its own sake, with faith, comes to for its own sake"@en, "Schelo lischma mit Glauben führt zu lischma"@de ;
    skos:definition "Through study even not lishmah, the Light in the Torah returns one to the good, so one comes to lishmah; for those with complete faith this is assured even without prior suffering."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:KabbalahAshlagShelloLishmaBeEmuna ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:KabbalahAshlagHaluqaGimelLishma ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:KabbalahAshlagShelloLishmaLishma (Haqdama, §31): there the passage is said of every engagement; here it is assured only to one of complete faith, through the Light in the Torah, and without the prior sufferings of the Mishna's way."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§11 (יא), 13 (יג), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagHaMaorShebaToraMahaziroLeMutav a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The Light in the Torah brings one back to the good"@en, "Das Licht in der Tora führt zum Guten zurück"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Talmudic sages replaced the Mishnaic ascetic means with the Torah's Light, said to be strong enough to reform the learner and bring him to lishmah by study alone."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: המאור שבה מחזירו למוטב (ha-maor she-bah machaziro le-mutav)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §11 (יא), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §12
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagMehusreiEmuna a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Learners not brought to lishma: they lack faith"@en, "Lernende ohne lischma: Glaubensmangel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Many learners did not come from shelo lishmah to lishmah; the reason given is that they lack faith, received no Light, walk in darkness and die without wisdom."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: מחוסרי אמונה (mechusrei emunah)."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that does not come about or is lost, and its cause. It names how pmp:KabbalahAshlagShelloLishmaBeEmuna fails or is lost."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§12 (יב), 13 (יג), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagMitharetAlYegiato a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sign of study shelo lishma: regret when no gain came"@en, "Zeichen von schelo lischma: Reue ohne Eigennutz"@de ;
    skos:definition "If after all the effort one learns that no private benefit came and one regrets the toil, this shows one had mixed in self-benefit from the start."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: מתחרט (mitcharet)."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that does not come about or is lost, and its cause. It names how pmp:KabbalahAshlagShelloLishmaBeEmuna fails or is lost."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §12 (יב), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagShelloLishmaPresupposesEmuna a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Faith before study not for its own sake can lead to lishma"@en, "Glaube als Bedingung für schelo lischma"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Light shines only for one with faith; for one dwelling in doubts the saying that shelo lishmah leads to lishmah does not apply, and the Torah becomes darkness and a potion of death."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:KabbalahAshlagShelloLishmaBeEmuna ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:KabbalahAshlagEmunaShlema ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "For one who dwells in doubt the Light does not shine; the Torah becomes darkness to him and a potion of death." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §12 (יב), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagMaorKeMiddatEmuna a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The Light in the measure of faith"@en, "Licht im Maß des Glaubens"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Light of Torah shines only for a believer, in proportion to how strong his faith is; holiness of faith purifies the eyes to enjoy God's light."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§12 (יב), 15 (טו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagEmunaShlema a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Complete faith"@en, "Vollständiger Glaube"@de ;
    skos:definition "Faith in God, His Torah and His providence of reward and punishment, held without reserve; it can be strengthened and enlarged by the Light of the Torah, and the measure of the Light received matches its strength."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: אמונה שלמה (emunah shlemah)."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§12 (יב), 17 (יז), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagSamaDeMota a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Torah without faith becomes a potion of death"@en, "Tora ohne Glauben wird Todesgift"@de ;
    skos:definition "For those lacking faith the Torah works in reverse: they receive darkness, their eyes darken, and their study becomes a deadly drug."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:KabbalahAshlagShelloLishmaBeEmuna ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: סמא דמותא (sama de-mota)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§12 (יב), 15 (טו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §14
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagToratoUmanuto a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Faith shown in the time given to Torah"@en, "Glaube sichtbar in der Torazeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Reading umanuto as emunato, the author holds how much faith a person has is visible in how much of his day he gives to Torah, like a lender's trust measured by the sum he risks."@en ;
    skos:note "The text grades faith by one hour, two hours and every free moment, after the lender who trusts with one coin, a hundred, half or all his wealth; only the last counts as complete."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §14 (יד), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagEinMazniahRegaMiTora a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sign of complete faith: no free moment left without Torah"@en, "Keine freie Minute ohne Tora"@de ;
    skos:definition "Allotting every free moment to Torah and divine service shows complete faith; allotting an hour or two shows partial faith."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: תורתו אומנותו (torato umanuto)."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: the text announces it as the mark of completion."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §14 (יד), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §15
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagYomHashemShekulloOr a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The Day of the Lord, all light"@en, "Der Tag des Herrn ganz Licht"@de ;
    skos:definition "When one knows in himself he has merited proper faith, he may expect the Light to bring him back and to reach the wholly luminous Day of the Lord."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: the text announces it as the mark of completion."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §15 (טו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagYomHashemPresupposesEmunaShlema a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Complete faith before the Light brings one back"@en, "Vollständiger Glaube vor dem Tag des Herrn"@de ;
    skos:definition "One must first be perfected in complete faith; for the faithless the light of the Day of the Lord turns into darkness."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:KabbalahAshlagHayyeiOsher ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:KabbalahAshlagEmunaShlema ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "For those lacking faith the light of the Day of the Lord turns to darkness, the potion of life to a potion of death." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §15 (טו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §16
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagQushiyatHaTosafot a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Resolving Tosafot's question on study not for its own sake"@en, "Lösung der Frage der Tosafot"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tosafot asked how study shelo lishmah can be a potion of death if one should study even shelo lishmah; the author distinguishes study for the commandment with faith in reward (leads to lishmah) from study for self-pleasure without such faith (deadly)."@en ;
    skos:note "Entered as a concept: the author answers a question of Tosafot (Taanit 7a) by a distinction and does not dispute them."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §16 (טז), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §17
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagLimudPresupposesHitHazzequtBeEmuna a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Strengthened faith before study"@en, "Glaubensstärkung vor dem Lernen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The learner is obliged before the study to strengthen faith; one who studies not for the commandment, not believing in reward and punishment, receives a potion of death."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:KabbalahAshlagShelloLishmaBeEmuna ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:KabbalahAshlagHitHazzequtBeEmunaLifneiHaLimud ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "One who studies not for the commandment, not believing in reward and punishment, receives the Torah as a potion of death; its light turns to darkness for him." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§16 (טז), 17 (יז), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmp:KabbalahAshlagHitHazzequtBeEmunaLifneiHaLimud a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Strengthening faith before study and aiming at the commandment of Torah"@en, "Glaubensstärkung vor dem Lernen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Before studying, the learner must strengthen himself in belief in God and in His providence that punishes and rewards, and direct his labour toward fulfilling the commandment of Torah study; then he benefits from its Light."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: לשם מצות התורה (le-shem mitzvat ha-Torah)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §17 (יז), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagHitHazzequtBeEmunaHagdalatHaEmuna a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Faith strengthened before study is enlarged by the Light"@en, "Glaubensstärkung vergrößert Glauben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Faith strengthened and toil aimed at the commandment of Torah lets one enjoy the Light, which further strengthens and enlarges the faith."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:KabbalahAshlagHitHazzequtBeEmunaLifneiHaLimud ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:KabbalahAshlagEmunaShlema ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §17 (יז), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagLimudLiZkotLeEmunaEmuna a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Study aimed at faith yields faith"@en, "Auf Glauben gerichtetes Lernen ergibt Glauben"@de ;
    skos:definition "One lacking faith who sets heart and mind to merit faith through Torah study has hope of reaching it."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:KabbalahAshlagLimudLiZkotLeEmuna ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:KabbalahAshlagEmunaShlema ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §17 (יז), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmp:KabbalahAshlagLimudLiZkotLeEmuna a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Studying Torah in order to merit faith"@en, "Torastudium, um Glauben zu erlangen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Even one who knows he has not yet attained faith may hope: let him set his heart and mind to merit faith in God through Torah study; this is called the greatest commandment and his only counsel."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: לזכות על ידה (lizkot al yadah)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §17 (יז), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagToraTavlin a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Torah as the spice made against the evil inclination"@en, "Tora als Gewürz gegen den bösen Trieb"@de ;
    skos:definition "Since God created the evil inclination and created Torah as its spice, sinners are not forced; anyone who fails has only himself to blame, otherwise Job's complaint would stand."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: תורה תבלין (Torah tavlin)."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:KabbalahAshlagTavlinimPeqihatEinayim (Haqdama, §40): there special spices break the husk and open the eyes; here the Torah itself is the spice created with the evil inclination, so that no sinner may plead compulsion."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§17 (יז), 18 (יח), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagToraTavlinMehiyatHaYetzer a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Study with toil and intention erases the evil inclination"@en, "Lernen mit Mühe und Absicht löscht den bösen Trieb"@de ;
    skos:definition "Torah as spice, studied with the owed toil and with heart set on drawing the Light, is said to weaken and wholly dissolve the evil inclination."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:KabbalahAshlagHamshakhatHaMaorShebaTora ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:KabbalahAshlagMehiyatHaYetzerHaRa ;
    skos:note "Inferred from the two failure reasons the author lists."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§17 (יז), 18 (יח), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §18
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagHirhureiAveraAharHaTavlin a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sinful thoughts remaining after the spice"@en, "Noch sündige Gedanken nach dem Gewürz"@de ;
    skos:definition "One who claims to have received the spice yet still has sinful thoughts and doubts, the evil inclination not dissolved, cannot excuse himself as forced; the cause is his own negligence."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: הרהורי עבירה (hirhurei averah)."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that does not come about or is lost, and its cause. It names how pmp:KabbalahAshlagShelloLishmaBeEmuna fails or is lost."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §18 (יח), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagYetzerHaRa a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The evil inclination"@en, "Der böse Trieb"@de ;
    skos:definition "The evil inclination was created by God together with its strength, and God also created the faithful remedy, Torah as spice, able to wear down and erase it; it also spreads nets of objections to catch innocent souls."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "yetzer ha-ra" ;
    pm:nameRole "the inclination created with its strength, against which the Torah is the remedy; it spreads nets for innocent souls" ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: יצה\"ר (yetzer ha-ra)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§18 (יח), 25 (כה), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagMehiyatHaYetzerHaRa a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The evil inclination erased"@en, "Auflösung des bösen Triebes"@de ;
    skos:definition "The state in which Torah, as the spice created against the evil inclination, has weakened and wholly erased it, so that the person is freed of sinful thoughts and doubts."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: נמוח היצה\"ר (nimoach ha-yetzer ha-ra)."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §18 (יח), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagHitrashlutBeKamut a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Evil inclination not removed: neglect in quantity"@en, "Böser Trieb bleibt: Nachlässigkeit in der Menge"@de ;
    skos:definition "If one studied Torah and did not remove the evil inclination, one reason is negligence in giving the toil owed to study."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: כמות (kamut)."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that does not come about or is lost, and its cause. It names how pmp:KabbalahAshlagHamshakhatHaMaorShebaTora fails or is lost."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §18 (יח), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmp:KabbalahAshlagHamshakhatHaMaorShebaTora a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Study that aims to draw the Light: quantity and quality"@en, "Lernen mit Absicht, das Licht zu ziehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Give the full measure of toil owed to Torah study (quantity), and throughout the study keep heart and mind on drawing down the Torah's Light, which plants belief in the heart, not letting attention drift from it even if it was intended at the start (quality)."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: להמשיך את המאור שבתורה (lehamshikh et ha-maor she-ba-Torah); כמות / איכות."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §18 (יח), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagHitrashlutBeEikhut a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Evil inclination not removed: neglect in quality"@en, "Böser Trieb bleibt: Nachlässigkeit in der Qualität"@de ;
    skos:definition "The other reason: the amount of toil was given but heart and mind were not set during study on drawing the Light that brings faith; they learned with distraction from the essential aim, even if they intended it at the start."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: איכות; הסח הדעת (eikhut; hessach ha-daat)."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that does not come about or is lost, and its cause. It names how pmp:KabbalahAshlagHamshakhatHaMaorShebaTora fails or is lost."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §18 (יח), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §19
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagTelunaAlHaRahu a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Answering those who wonder at Vital's advice"@en, "Verteidigung Vitals gegen Kritiker"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author removes the complaint of those who wonder at R. Chayim Vital's advice to leave Talmud for Kabbalah, first stating the apparent contradictions himself and then reading mazal as success in erasing the evil inclination."@en ;
    skos:note "A dispute entered as a concept: the opposing view is reported by the author and not read in a work of its own."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§19 (יט), 22 (כב), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagQabbalaPresupposesNigle a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Revealed Torah before Kabbalah, in Vital's words"@en, "Offenbare Tora vor Kabbala (Vital)"@de ;
    skos:definition "In Vital's words one should not go to the wisdom of Kabbalah before Torah, Mishnah and Talmud; Kabbalah lacking revealed Torah resembles a bodiless soul that has no deed, reckoning or reward; conversely Talmud without the secrets is like a body sitting in darkness."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:KabbalahAshlagEsekBeHokhmatHaQabbala ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:KabbalahAshlagSederHaLimudLefiHaRahu ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Kabbalah studied apart from the revealed Torah resembles a bodiless soul, lacking deed, reckoning and reward." ;
    skos:note "The text quotes Vital and then limits the rule: it holds while one has come to lishma or is still inside the span of three or five years (pmc:KabbalahAshlagQabbalaPresupposesMiluiKeres)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §19 (יט), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmp:KabbalahAshlagSederHaLimudLefiHaRahu a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Vital's order of study"@en, "Studienordnung nach Vital"@de ;
    skos:definition "In the quoted passage of R. Chayim Vital: first study Scripture, Mishnah and Talmud as far as one's mind can bear, then the wisdom of truth; one heavy in Talmud analysis should, after testing his fortune, leave it for the wisdom of truth; one quick in analysis must still devote an hour or two daily to analysing halakhah."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: חכמת המקרא והמשנה והתלמוד … חכמת האמת."@en ;
    skos:note "Quoted verbatim by the author from Vital's introduction to Shaar ha-Hakdamot / Etz Chayim and then interpreted."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §19 (יט), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagLadaatEtKono a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Knowing one's Maker through the wisdom of truth"@en, "Den Schöpfer erkennen durch die Weisheit der Wahrheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "In the passage of R. Chayim Vital the author adopts, the scholar who studies lishmah, after Scripture, Mishnah and Talmud, turns to know his Maker through the wisdom of truth."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: לדעת את קונו (lada'at et kono)."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §19 (יט), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §21
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagHokhmatHaTora a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The whole wisdom of Torah in the heart"@en, "Weisheit der Tora"@de ;
    skos:definition "Attaining the whole wisdom of Torah, which the midrash calls an easy thing for whoever fears God and does the words of Torah; the author holds it needs no prior talent, only intention of heart and time."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: חכמת התורה (chokhmat ha-Torah)."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §21 (כא), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagYiratHashemHokhmatHaTora a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Fear of God and doing Torah yield all its wisdom"@en, "Gottesfurcht und Tun ergeben alle Weisheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "By the virtue of fear of God and keeping the commandments alone, without prior distinction, one merits all the wisdom of Torah."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:KabbalahAshlagKiyyumHaToraKeHilkhata ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:KabbalahAshlagHokhmatHaTora ;
    skos:note "Midrash Rabbah, adopted by the author in §23."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §21 (כא), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §22
#

pmp:KabbalahAshlagEsekBeHokhmatHaQabbala a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Turning to Kabbalah study"@en, "Hinwendung zum Studium der Kabbala"@de ;
    skos:definition "One who has toiled in revealed Torah without the evil inclination being erased should set aside deep analysis of the revealed Torah and devote his whole time to Kabbalah, which is clothed in the names of God, so that he can aim mind and heart at God while learning without strain."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: העסק בחכמת הקבלה (ha-esek be-chokhmat ha-kabbalah)."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmp:KabbalahAshlagEsekBeSeferHaZohar (Haqdama, §68): there the study of the Zohar is prescribed for the generation's redemption; here Kabbalah study is prescribed to the individual who toiled in revealed Torah without erasing the evil inclination, because its subjects are clothed in the names of God and the mind can stay on Him while learning."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§22 (כב), 23 (כג), 26 (כו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagToraNigleLevushimGashmiyim a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Revealed Torah too material to hold the intention"@en, "Offenbare Tora zu stofflich für die Absicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "In revealed Torah, garbed in material topics like theft and damages, it is very hard to keep heart on God while studying, all the more for one heavy in Talmud analysis; so the Light is not drawn."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that does not come about or is lost, and its cause. It names how pmp:KabbalahAshlagShelloLishmaBeEmuna fails or is lost."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §22 (כב), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagHokhmatHaQabbalaLevushaBeShemot a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Kabbalah clothed in God's names: its subjects and God are one"@en, "Kabbala in Gottesnamen gekleidet"@de ;
    skos:definition "Because the wisdom of Kabbalah is clothed wholly in the names of God, analysis of its subjects and God are one, so the learner can keep heart and mind on God without effort, even if slow."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §22 (כב), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §23
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagSimanYafeHameshShanim a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Deadline: no good sign within five years, or three"@en, "Frist: kein gutes Zeichen in fünf (drei) Jahren"@de ;
    skos:definition "A student who saw no good sign in his study within five years (Rabbi Yose: three) will not see one; the failure is put down to lacking intention of heart, not talent, and the span counts as sufficient."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: סימן יפה במשנתו (siman yafe be-mishnato)."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that does not come about or is lost, and its cause. It names how pmp:KabbalahAshlagShelloLishmaBeEmuna and pmp:KabbalahAshlagHamshakhatHaMaorShebaTora fails or is lost."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§23 (כג), 25 (כה), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagZmanLehitragel a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Time needed to grow used to the Light"@en, "Zeit zur Gewöhnung an das Licht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Time is needed to habituate oneself to the Light of Torah; the author does not know how long and one could wait seventy years, so the baraita fixes five (or three) years as fully sufficient."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §23 (כג), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagHameshOShaloshShanim a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Five years after the first Tanna, three after R. Yose"@en, "Fünf gegen drei Jahre"@de ;
    skos:definition "The baraita sets five years for a good sign; Rabbi Yose says three; the author cites both without deciding."@en ;
    skos:note "A dispute entered as a concept: both sides are read only as the author cites them; the work they stand in was not opened."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §23 (כג), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagTiqvatShav a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Against deceiving oneself with vain hope"@en, "Gegen Selbsttäuschung durch eitle Hoffnung"@de ;
    skos:definition "After the set span without a good sign one should not fool oneself further with false hopes, nor sit in the same state waiting."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:KabbalahAshlagBehinatHaMazal ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §23 (כג), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmp:KabbalahAshlagBehinatHaMazal a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Testing one’s fortune and changing the device after the deadline"@en, "Prüfen des eigenen Glücks und Wechsel der Methode"@de ;
    skos:definition "Count how long one has studied shelo lishmah; if within five years (Rabbi Yose: three) one may still wait and hope; if the span has passed without a good sign, stop deceiving oneself and at once find another device to reach lishmah."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: בחן מזלו; תחבולה (bachan mazalo; tachbulah)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§23 (כג), 25 (כה), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagEsekBeQabbalaHokhmatHaTora a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Kabbalah study as the device to merit the wisdom of Torah"@en, "Kabbala als Mittel zur Weisheit der Tora"@de ;
    skos:definition "After the deadline the most successful device to come to lishmah and to the wisdom of Torah is said to be Kabbalah study."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:KabbalahAshlagEsekBeHokhmatHaQabbala ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:KabbalahAshlagHokhmatHaTora ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §23 (כג), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagTahbulaQerovaUVetuha a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Kabbalah as the near and sure device"@en, "Kabbala als nahe und sichere Methode"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author calls Kabbalah study the more successful, safer, near and certain device, sure of success, the easiest way adequate even for small minds."@en ;
    skos:note "Statement on how sure the method is."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§23 (כג), 36 (לו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §24
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagQabbalaPresupposesHalakhaLeMaase a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Practical law kept when one turns to Kabbalah"@en, "Praktische Halacha bleibt Voraussetzung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The advice to leave revealed Torah never concerns what must be known for practice; it must be reviewed so as not to stumble, since an ignorant man cannot be pious and an error in learning counts as wilful."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:KabbalahAshlagEsekBeHokhmatHaQabbala ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:KabbalahAshlagHalakhaLeMaase ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Without the practical law one stumbles in deed; an error of learning counts as wilful, and a single sinner ruins much good." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §24 (כד), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagLoAmHaAretzHasid a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "An ignorant man cannot be pious"@en, "Ein Unwissender kann nicht fromm sein"@de ;
    skos:definition "Practical halakhah must not be neglected, for an ignorant man is not pious, an error of learning counts as wilful, and a single sinner ruins much good."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:KabbalahAshlagHalakhaLeMaase ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §24 (כד), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmp:KabbalahAshlagHalakhaLeMaase a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Reviewing the practical law as far as needed"@en, "Ausreichende Wiederholung der praktischen Halacha"@de ;
    skos:definition "Whatever must be known for practice must be reviewed as much as needed not to stumble in deed; the release from revealed Torah concerns only deep analysis that does not issue in practice. Learning from digests is a possible leniency but doubtful."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: הלכה למעשה (halakhah le-maaseh)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §24 (כד), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagLimudMiQitzurim a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Learning the law from digests is doubtful"@en, "Halacha aus Kurzfassungen ist zweifelhaft"@de ;
    skos:definition "Knowing a law from the source differs from knowing it from a single survey in a digest; the leniency needs great examination."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:KabbalahAshlagHalakhaLeMaase ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §24 (כד), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §25
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagMikhmoreiHaYetzer a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "The objections are nets of the evil inclination"@en, "Einwände als Netze des bösen Triebes"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author warns that the opening objections against Kabbalah study are snares spread by the evil inclination to catch innocent souls."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:KabbalahAshlagEsekBeHokhmatHaQabbala ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §25 (כה), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagKeMaayanHaMitgabber a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sign of lishma: the secrets open without books"@en, "Geheimnisse ohne Bücher offenbart"@de ;
    skos:definition "The sign of real lishmah: the secrets of Torah open to one like a gushing spring with no need for books."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: the text announces it as the mark of completion."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §25 (כה), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagSimanYafe a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A good sign within the span"@en, "Gutes Zeichen innerhalb der Frist"@de ;
    skos:definition "A good sign in one's study appearing within five (three) years is the expected mark that the path is working; within the span one may still wait and hope."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: סימן יפה (siman yafeh)."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: the text announces it as the mark of completion."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §25 (כה), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §26
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagQabbalaPresupposesMiluiKeres a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Talmud and decisors first, while the span lasts"@en, "Zuerst Schas und Poskim, innerhalb der Frist"@de ;
    skos:definition "The rule to fill oneself first with Talmud and decisors is agreed by all, but only while one has attained lishmah or the three- or five-year span has not yet run out; afterwards one must try Kabbalah."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:KabbalahAshlagEsekBeHokhmatHaQabbala ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:KabbalahAshlagShelloLishmaBeEmuna ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    skos:note "The text sets the order and says nothing of what follows from skipping it; hence prescribed order."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §26 (כו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §27
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagSitreiToraVeTaameiTora a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Two parts of the wisdom of truth: secrets and reasons of Torah"@en, "Zwei Teile der Weisheit der Wahrheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "The wisdom of truth has the secrets of Torah (first three sefirot, head of the partzuf), forbidden except by hint, and the reasons of Torah (lower seven, body), permitted and a great commandment to reveal; the division applies at every scale from the end of Asiyah to Keter of Atzilut."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: סתרי תורה / טעמי תורה."@en ;
    skos:note "The lower seven are called reasons, literally tastes, after the verse on the palate that tastes food: the palate is Malkhut of the head, source of every taste."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §27 (כז), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmp:KabbalahAshlagMesiratSitreiToraBeRemiza a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Handing on the secrets of Torah only by hint"@en, "Weitergabe der Geheimnisse nur andeutend"@de ;
    skos:definition "The secrets of Torah (first three sefirot, head of the partzuf, Maaseh Merkavah and Bereshit) may be disclosed only by allusion, by a Kabbalist master to a recipient who understands of his own mind, handed only to the modest under known conditions not found in any written or printed book."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: סתרי תורה … ברמיזה (sitrei Torah … be-remizah)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§27 (כז), 30 (ל), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmp:KabbalahAshlagGiluyTaameiToraLaRabbim a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Disclosing the reasons of Torah to the many"@en, "Offenlegung der Gründe der Tora für die Vielen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The reasons of Torah (lower seven sefirot, body of the partzuf) may and should be disclosed, by writing and printing books for the public; this is a great commandment with boundless reward, on which the coming of the redeemer depends."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: טעמי תורה … לגלותם (taamei Torah … legalotam); התפשטות לימוד הקבלה לרבים."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§27 (כז), 30 (ל), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §28
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagAtiqYomin a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Atik Yomin, the Ancient of Days"@en, "Atik Jomin"@de ;
    skos:definition "Per Rashbam as quoted, the Ancient of Days is the Holy One; He covered the secrets of Torah, and He first covered then disclosed the reasons of Torah, granting permission to reveal them."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Atiq Yomin" ;
    pm:nameRole "the Holy One, who covered the secrets of Torah and covered then disclosed its reasons" ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: עתיק יומין (Atik Yomin)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§28 (כח), 30 (ל), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §29
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagKisuiSitreiToraSakhar a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Covering the secrets earns their attainer the reward"@en, "Verbergen der Geheimnisse wird belohnt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The attainer of the secrets of Torah receives the great reward of the verse for covering and not disclosing them."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:KabbalahAshlagMesiratSitreiToraBeRemiza ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:KabbalahAshlagHasagatSitreiToraVeTaameiTora ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §29 (כט), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagHasagatSitreiToraVeTaameiTora a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Attaining the secrets and the reasons of Torah"@en, "Erlangen der Geheimnisse und Gründe der Tora"@de ;
    skos:definition "The text speaks of one who attains (ha-masigam) the secrets of Torah, rewarded for covering them, and one who attains the reasons of Torah, rewarded for disclosing them to others."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: המשיג סתרי תורה / טעמי תורה (ha-masig sitrei Torah / taamei Torah)."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §29 (כט), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §30
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagSitreiToraPresupposesLibboDoeg a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "The secrets handed only to the worthy"@en, "Geheimnisse nur an Würdige"@de ;
    skos:definition "The secrets of Torah are passed solely to one whose heart is anxious within him, the modest, under known conditions; transgressing the ban on disclosure is named as one cause of past deviation."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:KabbalahAshlagHasagatSitreiToraVeTaameiTora ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:KabbalahAshlagMesiratSitreiToraBeRemiza ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Transgressing the sages’ words on what may not be disclosed is named as one of the two causes of past straying from the way of God." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§30 (ל), 37 (לז), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagKetivatSeferGiluy a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Writing a book is the widest disclosure"@en, "Ein Buch ist die weiteste Offenlegung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Writing a book is the widest possible disclosure, for its author cannot know who reads it and the fully wicked might look into it; hence printed books can contain only the permitted part."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:KabbalahAshlagGiluyTaameiToraLaRabbim ;
    skos:note "Used as argument that printed Kabbalah books hold only taamei Torah."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §30 (ל), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagGiluyLaRabbimBiatGoel a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Spreading Kabbalah to the many brings the redeemer"@en, "Verbreitung der Kabbala bringt den Erlöser"@de ;
    skos:definition "The coming of the righteous redeemer is said to depend on disclosing these lights to the many, specifically the many."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:KabbalahAshlagGiluyTaameiToraLaRabbim ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:KabbalahAshlagHamshakhatOrHaHesed ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:KabbalahAshlagLimudHaZoharGeula (Haqdama, §68): there the study of the Zohar and the inner Torah brings redemption; here the disclosure of the reasons of Torah to the many, and to the many alone, is what the redeemer's coming depends on."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §30 (ל), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §31
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagBukeiSeriqei a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against the popular nonsense about redemption"@en, "Gegen volkstümlichen Unsinn über die Erlösung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The masses are said to have hung unbearable absurdities on the Zohar's dependence of redemption on spreading Kabbalah; the author gives his own explanation."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: בוקי סריקי (bukei serikei)."@en ;
    skos:note "A dispute entered as a concept: the opposing view is reported by the author and not read in a work of its own."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §31 (לא), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagRuhaDeMalkaMeshiha a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The spirit of Messiah"@en, "König Messias und Geist des Messias"@de ;
    skos:definition "The spirit of Messiah is identified with the holy spirit and the spirit of Chokhmah and Binah; it hovers over those engaged in Torah in exile to awaken them to lishmah, and departs from those who make Torah dry; the Messiah appears once Israel draws the Light of Wisdom."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "ruha di-Meshiha" ;
    pm:nameRole "the spirit of hokhma and bina resting on the King Messiah, hovering over those who study Torah in exile" ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: רוחא דמשיח (rucha di-Meshicha)."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:KabbalahAshlagRuhaDeMashiah (Haqdama, §70): there the spirit is to bring Israel out of distress; here it is the Light of Wisdom clothed in the Light of Hesed, which hovers over learners in exile to wake them to lishma and departs from those who make the Torah dry."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§31 (לא), 34 (לד), 35 (לה), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §32
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagYiraVeAhavaAlMenatLeqabbelPeras a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Love and fear for reward are the maidservant's"@en, "Liebe und Furcht um Lohn sind die der Magd"@de ;
    skos:definition "Fear and love in Torah held on condition of reward are called the handmaid's, under which the earth trembles."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:KabbalahAshlagTorahUMitzvotAlMenatLeHashpia ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §32 (לב), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §33
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagShifha a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The maidservant, holy and of the husks"@en, "Die Magd (heilig / der Schalen)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Shelo lishmah study is the holy handmaid assisting and preparing for the mistress, ranked as the world of Asiyah of holiness; when it cannot lead to lishmah it passes to the impure handmaid of the shells who robs that Torah and inherits the mistress."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "shifha di-qedusha / shifha di-qelippa" ;
    pm:nameRole "study not for its own sake, serving the mistress or robbing her" ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: שפחה (shifchah)."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:KabbalahAshlagShifhaDeQedushaVeShifhaTmea (Haqdama, §31): there the holy maidservant is the second division of the work and the impure one confuses a person; here the maidservant is study not for its own sake itself, holy while it can lead to lishma and ranked as Assiya of holiness, and passing to the husks, who rob that Torah and inherit the mistress, when it cannot."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §33 (לג), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagShekhinaGevira a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The holy Shekhina, called earth and mistress"@en, "Die heilige Schechina"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Shekhinah is the mistress served by the holy handmaid, is called earth, trembles when the impure handmaid robs Torah, dwells among learners in exile in concealment, and grieves over learners."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "ha-Shekhina ha-qedosha, called eretz and gevira" ;
    pm:nameRole "the mistress whom study serves, present among learners in exile in concealment" ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: שכינה (Shekhinah)."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:KabbalahAshlagShekhinta (Haqdama, §70): there the Shekhina is the totality of the souls of Israel; here she is the mistress served by the holy maidservant, the earth that trembles when the impure one inherits her."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §33 (לג), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagShifhaYoreshetGevirta a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "The impure maidservant seizes Torah done without faith"@en, "Die unreine Magd raubt die Tora"@de ;
    skos:definition "Study done only because commanded, without complete faith, leaves the domain of the holy handmaid; the handmaid of the shells inherits and robs that Torah, carrying it to the shells, and the earth (Shekhinah) trembles."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:KabbalahAshlagShelloLishmaBeEmuna ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:KabbalahAshlagPahHaShifhaHaTmea (Haqdama, §31): there the snare catches whoever does not exert himself to come to lishma; here the cause is study without complete faith, whose Torah and service pass to the husks."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §33 (לג), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §34
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagHamshakhatOrHaHesed a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Drawing the Light of Hesed and in it the Light of Wisdom"@en, "Ziehen des Lichts von Chessed und Chochma"@de ;
    skos:definition "Israel as a whole is said to draw the upper Light of Chesed, called love of mercy, by engaging Torah without reward; in it the Light of upper Wisdom clothes itself, the spirit resting on the Messiah, after which the Messiah appears and the exiles are gathered."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: המשכת אור החסד / אור החכמה (hamshakhat or ha-chesed / or ha-chokhmah)."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §34 (לד), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagShelloAlMenatLeqabbelPerasOrHaHesed a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Torah without reward draws the Light of Hesed"@en, "Tora ohne Lohn zieht das Licht von Chessed"@de ;
    skos:definition "Engagement in Torah and commandments not for reward is what draws the upper Light of Chesed, in which the Light of Wisdom then clothes itself."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:KabbalahAshlagTorahUMitzvotAlMenatLeHashpia ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:KabbalahAshlagHamshakhatOrHaHesed ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§34 (לד), 36 (לו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagShevuatImTairu a pm:Sequencing ;
    rdfs:label "From Torah without reward to the ingathering of the exiles"@en, "Von lischma zur Sammlung der Verbannten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Torah without reward draws the Light of Hesed, and in that Hesed the Light of Wisdom is clothed as the spirit resting on the Messiah; the Messiah then appears and gathers the exiles."@en ;
    rdf:_1 pmp:KabbalahAshlagTorahUMitzvotAlMenatLeHashpia ;
    rdf:_2 pmc:KabbalahAshlagHamshakhatOrHaHesed ;
    rdf:_3 pmc:KabbalahAshlagRuhaDeMalkaMeshiha ;
    pm:seriesStatement "By the oath of the Song as the Tikkunim read it, Torah and commandments without reward draw the Light of Hesed; in it the Light of Wisdom is clothed as the spirit resting on the King Messiah; then he appears and gathers the exiles. The channels of holiness are ordered so, and the text admits no other way." ;
    skos:note "The source names a consequence of skipping the first stage, entered as pmc:KabbalahAshlagGeulaPresupposesLishma."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §34 (לד), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagGeulaPresupposesLishma a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Deeds without intent of reward before the full redemption"@en, "Lischma vor der vollständigen Erlösung"@de ;
    skos:definition "By the oath the Light of Chesed will not awaken until Israel's deeds are without intent of reward; the length of exile and suffering wait for this, and the full redemption and ingathering are impossible without it."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:KabbalahAshlagHamshakhatOrHaHesed ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:KabbalahAshlagTorahUMitzvotAlMenatLeHashpia ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Until the deeds of Israel are without intent of reward the Light of Hesed does not awaken; the exile and its sufferings wait, and the full redemption is impossible." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§34 (לד), 36 (לו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagGeulaTeluyaBeHitpashtutHaQabbala a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Redemption depends on spreading Kabbalah"@en, "Erlösung hängt an der Verbreitung der Kabbala"@de ;
    skos:definition "Light of Chesed drawn by Torah without reward carries the Light of Wisdom, the spirit on the Messiah; the ordering of the channels of holiness makes redemption impossible otherwise, and spreading Kabbalah to the many is the way."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: סדרי צנורות הקדושה."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§31 (לא), 34 (לד), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §35
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagToraNigleYevesha a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Revealed Torah dry for small minds"@en, "Offenbare Tora trocken für kleine Geister"@de ;
    skos:definition "Those who do not succeed through revealed Torah fail because for them it has no Light and is dry, because their minds are small."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that does not come about or is lost, and its cause. It names how pmp:KabbalahAshlagShelloLishmaBeEmuna fails or is lost."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §35 (לה), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagEsekBeQabbalaLishma a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Kabbalah study brings one to lishma"@en, "Kabbalastudium führt zu lischma"@de ;
    skos:definition "Kabbalah study, being clothed in God's names, is said to make it easy to draw the Light and to pass from shelo lishmah to lishmah."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:KabbalahAshlagEsekBeHokhmatHaQabbala ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:KabbalahAshlagHaluqaGimelLishma ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§22 (כב), 35 (לה), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagEsekBeQabbalaHashraatHaShekhina a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Kabbalah study prepares the indwelling of the Shekhina"@en, "Kabbalastudium bringt Geist und Schechina"@de ;
    skos:definition "Had they studied Kabbalah, God's spirit would hover above them and would prepare the indwelling of the Shekhinah."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:KabbalahAshlagEsekBeHokhmatHaQabbala ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:KabbalahAshlagLishmaHashraatHaShekhina ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §35 (לה), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §36
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagTaharaPresupposesQabbalaLeKhlalYisrael a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Kabbalah study for the whole people to reach that purity"@en, "Kabbala als Weg des ganzen Volkes"@de ;
    skos:definition "The whole people cannot reach this great purity other than by Kabbalah study; through revealed Torah alone only rare individuals with great toil can."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:KabbalahAshlagHamshakhatOrHaHesed ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:KabbalahAshlagEsekBeHokhmatHaQabbala ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "By the revealed Torah alone only rare individuals with great toil reach it, not most of the people." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §36 (לו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §37
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagGiluyDevarimAsurim a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "The danger of disclosing what is forbidden"@en, "Gefahr, Verbotenes zu enthüllen"@de ;
    skos:definition "One of two causes of past deviation from the way of God: transgressing the sages' words about matters forbidden to disclose."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:KabbalahAshlagMesiratSitreiToraBeRemiza ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: בדברים האסורים לגלות."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §37 (לז), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagHoraotGashmiyot a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "The danger of taking Kabbalah in a bodily sense"@en, "Gefahr der körperlichen Deutung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The second cause of deviation: grasping Kabbalistic words in their outward, material meaning and so transgressing the ban on images; this also built a wall around the wisdom."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:KabbalahAshlagEsekBeHokhmatHaQabbala ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: הוראות גשמיות (horaot gashmiyot)."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:KabbalahAshlagPesselUDmut (Haqdama, §58): there the fear of idol and image keeps the generation from the Zohar; here the bodily reading is named as one of two causes by which some did stray, and the wall around the wisdom."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §37 (לז), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagHomaBetzura a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Many began Kabbalah and could not go on"@en, "Viele begannen Kabbala und konnten nicht fortfahren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Many began Kabbalah but could not go on, failing to understand and put off by the bodily terms."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that does not come about or is lost, and its cause. It names how pmp:KabbalahAshlagEsekBeHokhmatHaQabbala fails or is lost."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §37 (לז), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagPanimMeirotUPanimMasbirot a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Panim Meirot u-Panim Masbirot: the author's commentary on Ez Hayyim"@en, "Panim Meirot u-Panim Masbirot"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author reports he laboured on this commentary to the Ari's Etz Chayim, stripping corporeal forms and recasting them as spiritual laws so beginners can follow by reason."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Yehuda Leib Ashlag, in the Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot" ;
    dcterms:date "1956"^^xsd:gYear ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: פנים מאירות ופנים מסבירות."@en ;
    skos:note "The ordering is the author’s: he arranges the material he expounds; the date is the first year of the edition read (Jerusalem, 1956-1966)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:compilerInference ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §37 (לז), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagHuqqeiHaRuhaniyim a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Spiritual laws above place and time"@en, "Geistige Gesetze jenseits von Ort und Zeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author's method strips the corporeal forms of Kabbalistic terms and sets them within spiritual laws above place and time."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §37 (לז), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagHavanaBeTaamamUNimuqam a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Understanding Kabbalah by its reasons, beyond place and time"@en, "Kabbala in geistigen Begriffen verstehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "With the author's commentary that strips the corporeal images, any beginner is said to grasp the subjects through their grounds with a clear mind, as easily as Gemara with Rashi."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: להבין בטעמם ונימוקם (lehavin be-taamam u-nimukam)."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §37 (לז), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §39
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagToratHayyim a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Lishma: for the Torah's sake, the Torah of life"@en, "Lischma heißt um der Tora willen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Since the Torah's name is Torah of life, lishmah means study that brings one life and length of days; intending only the Maker's contentment is not yet enough. One not aiming at this gets the opposite, a potion of death."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: תורת חיים (torat chayim)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §39 (לט), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §42
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagDevekutBeKholLevNefeshMeod a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Cleaving to Him with all heart, soul and might"@en, "Anhaften an Gott (Dewekut)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Once the one cause of distance, scant understanding of His providence, is removed, one is said to be freed at once of all sorrow and to cleave to Him with all heart, soul and might; on attaining revealed providence this cleaving follows of itself, and with revealed providence all would cleave to Him in love without a moment's break."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: להדבק בו ית' (lehidavek bo; devekut)."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:KabbalahAshlagDevekutHashvaatHaTzura (Petiha, §5): there adhesion is equivalence of form brought by the bestowing will; here it is the cleaving that follows of itself from attaining revealed providence, as complete repentance."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§42 (מב), 44 (מד), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagMiutHaHavanaBaHashgaha a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Scant understanding of providence as the root of all evil"@en, "Mangelndes Verständnis der Vorsehung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The sole cause of distance from God, of sins and suffering, is said to be our scant understanding of His providence; grasping it is what causes every good and it is the pole on which all turn."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: מיעוט ההבנה בהשגחתו."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§42 (מב), 44 (מד), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §43
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagHashgahaGeluyaTzaddiqimGemurim a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "With revealed providence all would be righteous"@en, "Mit offenbarer Vorsehung wären alle gerecht"@de ;
    skos:definition "If sin brought instant death and a commandment brought supreme pleasure, no one would sin or delay a commandment; all would be fully righteous."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §43 (מג), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §44
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagEhadMeElef a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Stumbling at every step: one in a thousand"@en, "Straucheln bei jedem Schritt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Because providence is hidden, not everyone who wishes to take the name may do so; one stumbles at every step, as a thousand enter the room and one emerges to teach."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:KabbalahAshlagKolAsherTimtzaYadkha ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §44 (מד), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §45
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagArbaBehinotHaHashgaha a pm:Sequencing ;
    rdfs:label "Four ways of perceiving providence"@en, "Vier Weisen der Vorsehung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Single hiding, hiding within hiding, providence of reward and punishment (repentance from fear) and eternal providence (repentance from love); the first three only prepare the fourth."@en ;
    rdf:_1 pmc:KabbalahAshlagHesterEhad ;
    rdf:_2 pmc:KabbalahAshlagHesterBetokhHester ;
    rdf:_3 pmc:KabbalahAshlagTeshuvaMiYira ;
    rdf:_4 pmc:KabbalahAshlagTeshuvaMeAhava ;
    pm:seriesStatement "The author numbers four ways in which people perceive providence, two of hiding (single hiding, hiding within hiding) and two of disclosure (reward and punishment, eternal providence); the first three are only preparations by which one merits the fourth, and whoever stands in a way is named by it: not wholly wicked, wholly wicked, intermediate, wholly righteous." ;
    skos:note "The source names a consequence of skipping, entered as pmc:KabbalahAshlagTeshuvaMeAhavaPresupposesShaloshHakhanot."@en ;
    skos:note "The same order recurs as the measures of the wicked, the intermediate and the righteous that every person passes (§§124, 129) and as the four holy worlds (§§149-150); those are not entered as series of their own."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§45 (מה), 64 (סד), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §47
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagPanimVeAhorayim a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The Face and the Back of God"@en, "Angesicht und Rücken Gottes"@de ;
    skos:definition "God's Face is His complete measure of goodness, disclosed when He benefits creatures; when they suffer only His Back is seen, and one may doubt whether it is He, as with a friend seen from behind."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "panim / ahorayim" ;
    pm:nameRole "His full goodness disclosed when He benefits His creatures, or only His back seen in their suffering" ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: פנים; אחוריים (panim; achorayim)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§47 (מז), 48 (מח), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §48
#

pmp:KabbalahAshlagHitHazzequtBeEmunaBeHesterPanim a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Strengthening faith while the Face is hidden"@en, "Glaubensstärkung in der Verhüllung"@de ;
    skos:definition "When God's goodness is hidden and suffering comes, one needs great strengthening in faith in Him in order to guard against sinful thoughts, since He is hard to recognise from behind."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §48 (מח), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §49
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagHesterBetokhHester a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Double hiding: suffering put down to chance, denial"@en, "Doppelte Verhüllung: Leid dem Zufall zugeschrieben"@de ;
    skos:definition "When suffering grows very great the hiding doubles: one no longer believes God is angry and punishing, attributes it to chance and nature, denies the providence that punishes and rewards, and turns to other gods; such sins count as wilful and he is called completely wicked."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: הסתר תוך הסתר; כפירה (hester be-tokh hester; kefirah)."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that does not come about or is lost, and its cause. It names how pmp:KabbalahAshlagKolAsherTimtzaYadkha fails or is lost."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§49 (מט), 52 (נב), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §51
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagHesterEhad a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Single hiding: sins as errors, not wholly wicked"@en, "Einfache Verhüllung: Sünden als Irrtümer"@de ;
    skos:definition "In single hiding one still believes suffering is punishment but, finding it hard to recognise God from behind, comes to sin; these count as errors and he is called not completely wicked."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: רשע שאינו גמור."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that does not come about or is lost, and its cause. It names how pmp:KabbalahAshlagHitHazzequtBeEmunaBeHesterPanim fails or is lost."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §51 (נא), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §53
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagLefumTzaaraAgra a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Choice and reward belong to the time of concealment"@en, "Wahl und Lohn gehören zur Verhüllung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The work of Torah by choice operates mainly in the two hidden modes, where one can always choose; reward is by the measure of pain. Concealment is a passage, not perfection, given intentionally so humans may toil by choice."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: לפום צערא אגרא; מעבר (ma'avar)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§53 (נג), 80 (פ), 81 (פא), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmp:KabbalahAshlagKolAsherTimtzaYadkha a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Doing all in one's power during the concealment"@en, "Alles in eigener Kraft Mögliche tun"@de ;
    skos:definition "During the time of hidden providence one must exert and do everything one's hand and strength can do, by choice and strengthening in faith, since one will not merit the disclosure before that; reward is by the measure of pain."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: כל אשר תמצא ידך (kol asher timtza yadkha)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§53 (נג), 54 (נד), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagGiluyPanimPresupposesYegiaShlema a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "All effort before the disclosure of the Face"@en, "Volle Mühe vor der Enthüllung"@de ;
    skos:definition "One will not merit disclosure of the Face before exerting and doing all that is in his hand."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:KabbalahAshlagGiluyPanim ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:KabbalahAshlagKolAsherTimtzaYadkha ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "The Face is not disclosed to one who has not first done all within his hand and power." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §53 (נג), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §54
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagYegiaBeHesterGiluyPanim a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Effort completed in concealment brings revealed providence"@en, "Vollendete Mühe bringt offenbare Vorsehung"@de ;
    skos:definition "When God sees that the person has completed his measure of toil by choice and strengthening in faith, He helps him and he attains revealed providence."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:KabbalahAshlagHitHazzequtBeEmunaBeHesterPanim, pmp:KabbalahAshlagKolAsherTimtzaYadkha ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:KabbalahAshlagGiluyPanim ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §54 (נד), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagGiluyPanim a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Revealed providence: the disclosure of the Face"@en, "Erlangung der offenbaren Vorsehung (Enthüllung des Angesichts)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Perceiving God's providence openly fitting His name as the Good One who benefits; it comes in two degrees (reward and punishment; eternal providence) and is the finding promised to those who toil in Torah."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: גילוי פנים; השגחה גלויה (giluy panim; hashgachah geluyah)."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§54 (נד), 95 (צה), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §55
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagTeshuvaMiYira a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "First degree: clear perception of reward and punishment, repentance from fear"@en, "Erste Stufe: Vorsehung von Lohn und Strafe (Umkehr aus Furcht)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Clearly attaining the reward of each commandment for the world to come and tasting its delight at once, and feeling the bitter taste of each sin while alive; one is then sure not to sin again. This is repentance from fear, by which wilful sins become as errors; the person is called incomplete righteous and intermediate (beinoni)."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: תשובה מיראה; השגת השגחת שכר ועונש (teshuvah mi-yirah)."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "It comes by way of the eyes being opened in Torah (§§83, 87, 89)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§55 (נה), 57 (נז), 63 (סג), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagTaanugBeMitzva a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sign: delight in each commandment, bitterness in each sin"@en, "Wonne in jedem Gebot, Bitterkeit in jeder Sünde"@de ;
    skos:definition "At the first degree one tastes the wondrous pleasure of a commandment at once while doing it and feels the bitter taste of sin while alive, the certain future reward counting as already collected."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: the text announces it as the mark of completion."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§55 (נה), 84 (פד), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §56
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagYodeaTaalumot a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The Knower of hidden things"@en, "Der Kenner des Verborgenen"@de ;
    skos:definition "God as Knower of secrets testifies about the penitent; His salvation, which gives clear perception of punishment and reward, is itself termed testimony."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Yodea taalumot" ;
    pm:nameRole "God, whose salvation by the disclosure of the Face testifies that the penitent will not return to folly" ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: יודע תעלומות (yodea taalumot)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §56 (נו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagYaidAlavYodeaTaalumot a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sign of complete repentance: the Knower of secrets testifies"@en, "Der Kenner des Verborgenen bezeugt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The sages gave a clear sign of complete repentance: that the Knower of hidden things testifies one will not return to folly, i.e. attaining disclosure of the Face, whose salvation assures one will not sin again."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: עד שיעיד עליו יודע תעלומות (ad she-yaid alav yodea taalumot)."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: the text announces it as the mark of completion."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:KabbalahAshlagTeshuvaBiQviutMuhletet (Haqdama, §51): there the testimony marks repentance fixed for good, after Maimonides; here the testimony is itself the disclosure of the Face, God's salvation, which alone makes one sure not to sin again."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §56 (נו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §58
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagZedonotKeShegagot a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Why repentance from fear makes wilful sins as errors"@en, "Warum Furchtumkehr Sünden zu Irrtümern macht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Wilful sins stem from double hiding (disbelief in reward and punishment); attaining that providence shows retroactively that one erred bitterly, so they become like errors of single hiding but not erased."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§58 (נח), 59 (נט), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagHirhureiAveraBeHesterEhad a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Sinful thoughts under the hidden Face"@en, "Sündige Gedanken in der Verhüllung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Under single hiding the abundance of suffering can bring sinful thoughts and confusion of mind, since God is seen only from behind and one may doubt whether it is He."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:KabbalahAshlagHitHazzequtBeEmunaBeHesterPanim ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§51 (נא), 58 (נח), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §60
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagHesterEhadLoNitqan a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Repentance from fear leaves the past single hiding unmended"@en, "Umkehr aus Furcht heilt die Vergangenheit nicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Repentance from fear repairs the double hiding (wilful sins become errors) but not the earlier single hiding and its errors, so one is not yet completely righteous and the past still needs repair."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that does not come about or is lost, and its cause. It names how pmc:KabbalahAshlagTeshuvaMiYira fails or is lost."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§60 (ס), 61 (סא), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §61
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagTzaddiqVeBeinoni a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Righteous as justifying providence; intermediate between fear and love"@en, "Gerecht heißt die Vorsehung rechtfertigen"@de ;
    skos:definition "One who attains disclosure of the Face is called righteous because he justifies providence as it truly is, doing perfect good to bad and good; intermediate (beinoni) is between fear and love."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: צדיק; בינוני (tzaddik; beinoni)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§61 (סא), 62 (סב), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §64
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagTeshuvaMeAhava a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Second degree: eternal providence, repentance from love"@en, "Zweite Stufe: ewige Vorsehung (Umkehr aus Liebe)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Attaining the true eternal providence in which God benefits the bad and the good alike; this is repentance from love, wilful sins turn into merits, the person keeps all 613 commandments in love and fear and is called completely righteous."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: תשובה מאהבה; השגחת הנצחיות (teshuvah me-ahavah)."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§64 (סד), 90 (צ), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagTeshuvaMeAhavaPresupposesShaloshHakhanot a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "The first three ways prepare the fourth"@en, "Die ersten drei Weisen bereiten die vierte vor"@de ;
    skos:definition "Double hiding, single hiding and reward-and-punishment are only preparations by which one merits the fourth, eternal providence; before repentance from fear one was not fit even to prepare for love."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:KabbalahAshlagTeshuvaMeAhava ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:KabbalahAshlagTeshuvaMiYira ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Before repentance from fear one is not fit even to prepare oneself for repentance from love." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§62 (סב), 64 (סד), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §66
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagMitzvatHaAhava a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The commentators on the commandment to love"@en, "Die Kommentatoren zum Liebesgebot"@de ;
    skos:definition "Commentators asked how Torah can command love, which cannot be compelled, and answered that love follows from keeping 612 commandments; the author says this needs broad explanation and finally that the question is no question, since love comes by toil to revealed providence."@en ;
    skos:note "A dispute entered as a concept: the opposing view is reported by the author and not read in a work of its own."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§66 (סו), 67 (סז), 98 (צח), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagTaryabMitzvotAhava a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "The 612 commandments yield love, after the commentators"@en, "612 Gebote ergeben Liebe"@de ;
    skos:definition "The commentators hold love of God is drawn of itself to one who keeps the 612 commandments properly."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:KabbalahAshlagTaryabMitzvot ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:KabbalahAshlagAhavatHashem ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §66 (סו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmp:KabbalahAshlagTaryabMitzvot a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Keeping the 612 commandments so that love follows"@en, "Halten der 612 Gebote, damit Liebe folgt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The commentators answered that by compelling oneself to keep all 612 commandments properly, love of God comes of itself; the author accepts it as needing much wider explanation."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: תרי\"ב המצוות."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §66 (סו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §68
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagNetiyotLeAvodatHashem a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The natural traits made for the service of God"@en, "Natürliche Eigenschaften für den Dienst geschaffen"@de ;
    skos:definition "All natural inclinations used toward fellows were implanted for their final role in serving God; the world was prepared so they develop through dealings with creatures until they become vessels of service; hence each person is bound to say the world exists for his sake."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §68 (סח), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §69
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagAhavatHashem a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Love of God"@en, "Gottesliebe in vier Maßen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Love of God follows the four measures of human love: dependent love (first despite past harms, then with no harm ever) and independent love (first not yet knowing all the beloved's dealings, then eternal absolute love after knowing them all); in love of God these become causally linked degrees."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: אהבה התלויה בדבר / שאינה תלויה בדבר (ahavah ha-teluyah be-davar)."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§69 (סט), 74 (עד), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §70
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagAhavaTeluyaMiddaAlef a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "First measure: dependent love despite past harms"@en, "Erstes Maß: abhängige Liebe trotz früherer Schäden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Love that depends on a thing, arising from much good and benefit received, where before the two knew and loved each other they did each other harm and choose not to remember it, since love covers all transgressions."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: אהבה התלויה בדבר (ahava ha-teluya be-davar)."@en ;
    skos:note "Member of a series written by the integrator; the first pass held the four measures in one capacity record."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §70 (ע), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagAhavaTeluyaMiddaBet a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Second measure: dependent love with no harm ever"@en, "Zweites Maß: abhängige Liebe ohne je einen Schaden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Dependent love where the two have only ever done each other good and no trace of damage or evil has ever stood between them; toward God it comes with repentance from love, when the sins are turned into merits."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: מידה ב' (midda bet)."@en ;
    skos:note "Member of a series written by the integrator; the first pass held the four measures in one capacity record."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§70 (ע), 109 (קט), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §72
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagAhavaSheEinaTeluyaMiddaAlef a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Third measure: independent love not yet knowing all"@en, "Drittes Maß: unabhängige Liebe, die noch nicht alles kennt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Love that depends on nothing, from knowing the beloved's surpassing worth, but before one knows all his dealings with others, some of which might seem on the surface to harm them; toward God it is love not yet eternal, since one has tipped oneself but not the world."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: אהבה שאינה תלויה בדבר (ahava she-eina teluya be-davar)."@en ;
    skos:note "Member of a series written by the integrator; the first pass held the four measures in one capacity record."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §72 (עב), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §73
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagAhavaNitzhit a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Fourth measure: eternal and absolute love"@en, "Viertes Maß: ewige und unbedingte Liebe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Independent love after one knows every dealing of the beloved with every person and finds no flaw but goodness beyond measure; toward God it is reached when one knows His providence over every creature as the Good One benefiting bad and good alike, and it is the world of Atzilut."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: אהבה נצחית ומוחלטת (ahava nitzhit u-muhletet)."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Member of a series written by the integrator; the first pass held the four measures in one capacity record."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§73 (עג), 121 (קכא), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §74
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagAhavaPresupposesMiddaRishona a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "No measure of love before the first"@en, "Jedes Maß der Liebe vor dem nächsten"@de ;
    skos:definition "In love of God the four measures are cause and effect: none can be attained before the first measure of dependent love is complete, and each completed measure causes the next."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:KabbalahAshlagAhavaTeluyaMiddaBet ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:KabbalahAshlagAhavaTeluyaMiddaAlef ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "No measure of love can be attained before the first measure of dependent love is complete." ;
    skos:note "The text says it of every later measure; the pair names the first step."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §74 (עד), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagArbaMiddotHaAhava a pm:Sequencing ;
    rdfs:label "Four measures of love as causal degrees"@en, "Vier Liebesmaße als Stufen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Dependent love despite past harms, dependent love with no harm ever, independent love not yet knowing all the beloved's dealings, and eternal, absolute love."@en ;
    rdf:_1 pmc:KabbalahAshlagAhavaTeluyaMiddaAlef ;
    rdf:_2 pmc:KabbalahAshlagAhavaTeluyaMiddaBet ;
    rdf:_3 pmc:KabbalahAshlagAhavaSheEinaTeluyaMiddaAlef ;
    rdf:_4 pmc:KabbalahAshlagAhavaNitzhit ;
    pm:seriesStatement "The four measures of love between people hold toward God as degrees of cause and effect: none is reached before the first measure of dependent love is complete, and each completed measure brings about the next, up to the eternal love." ;
    skos:note "The source names a consequence of skipping, entered as pmc:KabbalahAshlagAhavaPresupposesMiddaRishona."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §74 (עד), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §78
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagPeqihatEinayimBaTora a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Opening of the eyes in Torah: seeing one’s world while alive"@en, "Öffnung der Augen in der Tora"@de ;
    skos:definition "Through wondrous attainment in Torah, granted by God's salvation, one's eyes are opened to see in each commandment already kept the reward prepared for the world to come and the loss in each sin; this is the blessing of beholding one's world while still alive."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: פקיחת עינים בתורה; עולמך תראה בחייך (pekichat einayim ba-Torah)."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:KabbalahAshlagPeqihatEinayimLeMadregotHaHokhma (Haqdama, §40): there the eyes open to oneself and to the degrees of wisdom after the spices break the husk; here the opening is in the Torah, by God's salvation, and shows in each commandment kept the reward prepared for the world to come."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§78 (עח), 83 (פג), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmp:KabbalahAshlagTehiBeEinekhaKeRasha a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Holding oneself wicked until the eyes are opened; examining oneself"@en, "Sich für einen Frevler halten bis zur Augenöffnung"@de ;
    skos:definition "By the oath on the soul before birth, even if all the world calls one righteous one must count oneself wicked in one's own eyes so long as one has not merited opening of the eyes in Torah, and not be fooled by fame; yet one is also obliged to investigate in oneself whether one is completely righteous."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: תהיה בעיניך כרשע (tihyeh be-einekha ke-rasha)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§78 (עח), 88 (פח), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §80
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagMalakhimBliBehira a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The angels above, without choice"@en, "Die Engel"@de ;
    skos:definition "The angels are said to have no choice and to be compelled in their missions, so God has more contentment from human service done by choice."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "malakhim" ;
    pm:nameRole "servants without choice, compelled in their missions" ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: מלאכים (malakhim)."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:KabbalahAshlagMalakhim (Haqdama, §42): there the angels are the animal level of each world serving the souls; here they lack choice, so God has more contentment from service done by choice."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §80 (פ), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §82
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagGiluyPanimPresupposesMaavar a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Everyone must pass the corridor of concealment"@en, "Jeder muss durch den Durchgang der Verhüllung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Every person must pass through the time of hidden Face; all reward of commandments is earned only from toil in that time, after which revealed providence is attained."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:KabbalahAshlagGiluyPanim ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:KabbalahAshlagKolAsherTimtzaYadkha ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "All reward of the commandments is earned only by toil in the time of concealment; without passing it no one comes to revealed providence." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§81 (פא), 82 (פב), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagLifneiGiluyPanimEinShlemut a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Before the disclosure one cannot keep even the 612"@en, "Vor der Enthüllung kein Freisein von Sünde"@de ;
    skos:definition "Before disclosure of the Face, even seeing the back, one cannot avoid coming to sin sometimes; one cannot keep all 613 since love is not forced, nor even the 612 since one's fear is not fixed."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that does not come about or is lost, and its cause. It names how pmp:KabbalahAshlagKolAsherTimtzaYadkha and pmp:KabbalahAshlagYegiaLimtzoOrPanim fails or is lost."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §82 (פב), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagToraGimatriaTaryaAhorayim a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Torah is 611: the back"@en, "Tora = 611: der Rücken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Torah in gematria is 611, and every gematria alludes to the back, hinting that before disclosure one cannot keep even 612 properly."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §82 (פב), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §83
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagYegiaBaToraPeqihatEinayim a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Toil in Torah brings the opening of the eyes"@en, "Mühe in der Tora bringt Augenöffnung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Toil in Torah is said to lead, by God's salvation, to opening of eyes in Torah and so to the first degree of disclosure."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:KabbalahAshlagYegiaLimtzoOrPanim ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:KabbalahAshlagPeqihatEinayimBaTora ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§83 (פג), 93 (צג), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §84
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagKolHaOmedLigbot a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "What stands to be collected counts as collected"@en, "Gewissheit des Gewinns gilt als Gewinn"@de ;
    skos:definition "Whatever stands to be collected counts as collected: like a merchant sure of profit, clear attainment of future reward gives full joy now."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: כל העומד לגבות כגבוי דמי."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §84 (פד), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §85
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagTeshuvaMiYiraTeshuvaMeAhava a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Cleaving to Torah after the first degree leads to repentance from love"@en, "Erste Stufe führt allmählich zur Umkehr aus Liebe"@de ;
    skos:definition "The great cleaving to Torah and good deeds of one at the first degree helps him little by little to repentance from love and to keeping all 613."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:KabbalahAshlagYegiaLimtzoOrPanim ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:KabbalahAshlagTeshuvaMeAhava ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§85 (פה), 90 (צ), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §87
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagYiraShlemaPresupposesPeqihatEinayim a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Complete fear only after the opening of the eyes"@en, "Vollständige Furcht erst nach der Augenöffnung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Complete fear, such that the Knower of secrets testifies one will not return to folly, is not conceivable before full and clear perception of the providence that punishes and rewards, through opening of eyes; love is wholly beyond one's power before then."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:KabbalahAshlagTeshuvaMiYira ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:KabbalahAshlagPeqihatEinayimBaTora ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Before clear perception of reward and punishment by the opening of the eyes, complete fear is not conceivable at all, and love lies wholly beyond one’s power." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §87 (פז), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §88
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagLoLehaaminLaOlam a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Not to be fooled by the world's praise"@en, "Sich nicht vom Lob der Welt täuschen lassen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Since love and fear are known only to the person himself, and human nature trusts the world, one seen complete in 611 commandments is likely to fall into bitter error; hence the oath."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:KabbalahAshlagTehiBeEinekhaKeRasha ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §88 (פח), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §89
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagKiyyumHaToraPresupposesReiyatSakhar a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Seeing the reward while alive, to keep Torah as it should be kept"@en, "Lohn im Leben sehen ist nötig"@de ;
    skos:definition "Seeing and feeling the future reward with full clarity while still alive is necessary for keeping Torah properly so that the Knower of secrets testifies one will not return to folly."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:KabbalahAshlagKiyyumHaToraKeHilkhata ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:KabbalahAshlagPeqihatEinayimBaTora ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Unless one sees and knows the coming reward clearly while still alive, one cannot keep Torah and commandments so fully that the Knower of secrets testifies one will not return to folly." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §89 (פט), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §91
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagHaseraMitzvaAhat a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Still lacking one commandment: love"@en, "Noch fehlt ein Gebot: Liebe"@de ;
    skos:definition "One at the third mode is still called incomplete because he lacks the commandment of love and must complete the count of 613, the opening step at the doorway of perfection."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that does not come about or is lost, and its cause. It names how pmc:KabbalahAshlagTeshuvaMiYira fails or is lost."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §91 (צא), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §93
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagYagatiUMatzati a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Finding means finding the Face"@en, "Finden heißt das Angesicht finden"@de ;
    skos:definition "In I toiled and I found, the labour belongs to Torah while the finding is disclosure of the Face of providence, something beyond acquiring Torah; hence finding and not acquiring."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: יגעתי ומצאתי (yagati u-matzati)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §93 (צג), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §94
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagLoYagatiUMatzati a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Against expecting to find without toil"@en, "Gegen Finden ohne Mühe"@de ;
    skos:definition "The sages warn not to believe one who says he did not toil yet found, against a reading of the verse that even a lesser person who gives no toil will find."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:KabbalahAshlagYegiaLimtzoOrPanim ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §94 (צד), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagMetziaPresupposesYegia a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Toil indispensable for finding"@en, "Mühe ist für das Finden unerlässlich"@de ;
    skos:definition "Though the verse promises whoever seeks finds, one should not think a lesser person unwilling to toil will find; the sages warned toil is necessary."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:KabbalahAshlagGiluyPanim ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:KabbalahAshlagYegiaLimtzoOrPanim ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "One who does not toil does not find; the sages say not to believe him who says he found without toil." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §94 (צד), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §95
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagMelekhHayyim a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The King of Life"@en, "Der König des Lebens"@de ;
    skos:definition "God is the wellspring of every life and good, and life flows to branches cleaving to Him; the light of His face is what the toiler finds in Torah."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Melekh hayyim" ;
    pm:nameRole "the wellspring of every life and good, whose face's light the one who toils finds in Torah" ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: מלך חיים (melekh chayim)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §95 (צה), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §96
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagBorehMeHaAveraKeMeEsh a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sign: fleeing sin as from fire, unable to forgo a commandment"@en, "Flucht vor der Sünde wie vor Feuer"@de ;
    skos:definition "Those who reached revealed providence can no more keep from a commandment than from a wonderful pleasure, and flee sin as from a fire."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: the text announces it as the mark of completion."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§85 (פה), 96 (צו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagHaAnafDavuqBeShorsho a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Life flowing to the branch that cleaves to its root"@en, "Leben aus der Quelle"@de ;
    skos:definition "Those who laboured and found the radiance of His face cleave as branches to their root; His love reaches them as innate love along the channels nature gave man and life flows to them without break, which is why Torah is called life."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: חיים; הענף דבוק בשרשו (chayim; ha-anaf davuk be-shorsho)."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §96 (צו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §97
#

pmp:KabbalahAshlagYegiaLimtzoOrPanim a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Toil in Torah aimed at the radiance of the Face"@en, "Mühe in der Tora, um das Licht des Angesichts zu finden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Every person, while engaged in Torah, must toil in it and set mind and heart to find there the radiance of the King of Life's face, i.e. the attainment of revealed providence; nothing is lacking but the toil, and this aim is what lishmah means."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: אור פני מלך חיים (or penei melekh hayyim)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §97 (צז), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagYegiaLishmaSamHayyim a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Toil aimed at life makes one's Torah a potion of life"@en, "Mühe lischma macht die Tora zum Lebenstrank"@de ;
    skos:definition "Setting mind and heart to merit life makes one's Torah a potion of life."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:KabbalahAshlagYegiaLimtzoOrPanim ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:KabbalahAshlagHaAnafDavuqBeShorsho ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §97 (צז), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §98
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagMitzvatHaAhavaBeYadenu a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The commandment of love is in our hands"@en, "Das Liebesgebot liegt in unserer Macht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Love is fully in our hands because anyone can toil in Torah until he finds revealed providence, after which love comes of itself."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §98 (צח), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagGiluyPanimAhavaBeTzinorot a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Toil to revealed providence yields love through the natural channels"@en, "Offenbare Vorsehung ergibt Liebe auf natürlichen Wegen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Once revealed providence is attained, love comes on its own along the natural channels; hence the commandment of love is fully in our hands via toil."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:KabbalahAshlagYegiaLimtzoOrPanim ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:KabbalahAshlagAhavatHashem ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §98 (צח), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagEinoMaaminBeDivreiHazal a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Doubting that toil suffices is disbelief in the sages"@en, "Zweifel an der Mühe ist Unglaube"@de ;
    skos:definition "Whoever doubts that his own toil can bring him to this, for whatever reason, is said thereby not to believe the sages' words."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:KabbalahAshlagYegiaLimtzoOrPanim ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §98 (צח), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §100
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagHesterKediSheYevaqshuhu a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "He hides in order to be sought"@en, "Gott verbirgt sich, um gesucht zu werden"@de ;
    skos:definition "The hiding of the Face is not God's wish to remain hidden but like one who hides so his friend will search and find him; without initial concealment there would be no access to the light of His face."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §100 (ק), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §101
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagToraMakhbidaHesterPanim a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Much Torah makes the concealment heavier"@en, "Viel Tora macht die Verhüllung schwerer"@de ;
    skos:definition "Before disclosure, the Torah and commandments one has multiplied make the hiding heavier, since one who deems himself undeserving finds it hard to judge God favourably; this weight is the Torah's herald urging him to hurry and give the required toil."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:KabbalahAshlagYegiaLimtzoOrPanim ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: כרוזים (kruzim)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §101 (קא), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §102
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagShelloLishmaHesterBetokhHester a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Study not aimed at the Face deepens the concealment"@en, "Lernen ohne Ausrichtung vertieft die Verhüllung"@de ;
    skos:definition "One who studies shelo lishmah not only stays in hiding but his growing Torah adds concealment until he falls to hiding within hiding, called death, wholly cut from his root."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:KabbalahAshlagShelloLishmaBeEmuna, pmp:KabbalahAshlagYegiaLimtzoOrPanim ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §102 (קב), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §103
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagNigleVeNistar a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Hidden and revealed Torah: names of hiding and revealing"@en, "Verborgene und offenbare Tora"@de ;
    skos:definition "The hidden Torah is so called because God hides in Torah; the revealed because He is revealed through it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §103 (קג), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagGiluyPanimPresupposesToratHaNistar a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Attaining the Torah begins in the secret and ends in the plain sense"@en, "Ordnung: zuerst Geheimnis, dann einfacher Sinn"@de ;
    skos:definition "Kabbalists and the Gra's Siddur state that attaining Torah begins with sod and ends with peshat: through toil first in the hidden Torah one merits the revealed Torah."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:KabbalahAshlagGiluyPanim ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:KabbalahAshlagEsekBeHokhmatHaQabbala ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    skos:note "The text sets the order and says nothing of what follows from skipping it; hence prescribed order."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §103 (קג), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §105
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagYissurinPegamBaAhava a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Past suffering remains a blemish in love"@en, "Vergangenes Leid bleibt ein Makel"@de ;
    skos:definition "The suffering endured under the hidden Face, though one prefers not to recall it, is a great blemish even in love between people, and more so toward the truth of providence."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that does not come about or is lost, and its cause. It names how pmc:KabbalahAshlagTeshuvaMiYira fails or is lost."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §105 (קה), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §106
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagZedonotKeZekhuyot a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sign of repentance from love: wilful sins turned into merits"@en, "Absichtliche Sünden werden Verdienste"@de ;
    skos:definition "The mark of repentance from love: God not only forgives but turns every sin into a commandment."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: the text announces it as the mark of completion."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §106 (קו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §107
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagHitHapkhutHaYissurinLeSimha a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Past suffering turned to joy: the second measure of love"@en, "Umkehr aus Liebe verwandelt Leid in Freude"@de ;
    skos:definition "When wilful sins become merits, every past pain becomes cause and preparation for a commandment with eternal reward, so all sorrow turns to joy, and second-measure dependent love is reached."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§107 (קז), 109 (קט), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagSasVeSameahAlHaYissurin a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sign: rejoicing over all past suffering"@en, "Freude über alles vergangene Leid"@de ;
    skos:definition "One who repented from love rejoices over all the bitter pains and troubles he underwent, since they brought the sins now turned into commandments."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: the text announces it as the mark of completion."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §107 (קז), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §110
#

pmp:KabbalahAshlagHatzyoHayyavVeHatzyoZakkai a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Seeing oneself as half liable, half acquitted"@en, "Sich als halb schuldig, halb verdienstvoll sehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Addressed to one who has reached repentance from fear and feels fully righteous: he should picture the moment of his repentance as standing at the midpoint of his years, the half before still guilty and the half after meritorious, so that he knows he lacks one commandment, love."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: חציו חייב וחציו זכאי (hetzyo hayyav ve-hetzyo zakkai)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§110 (קי), 115 (קטו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §111
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagTannaQammaVeRabbiElazar a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The first Tanna and R. Elazar son of R. Shimon, and Rashi"@en, "Tanna Kamma gegen R. Elasar b. R. Schimon, und Raschi"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author finds the baraita puzzling and Rashi's reading (R. Elazar adds that one should see the world too as half and half) lacking the essential; he explains Tanna Kamma addresses love's second and third measures and R. Elazar of the fourth, which requires tipping the whole world."@en ;
    skos:note "A dispute entered as a concept: both sides are read only as the author cites them; the work they stand in was not opened."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§111 (קיא), 118 (קיח), 121 (קכא), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §116
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagHakhraaLeKhafZekhut a pm:Sequencing ;
    rdfs:label "From half and half to tipping the whole world"@en, "Sich selbst, dann die Welt neigen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Repentance from fear leaves one intermediate, half and half; the one commandment of love tips oneself to merit; tipping the whole world gives the fourth, eternal love."@en ;
    rdf:_1 pmc:KabbalahAshlagTeshuvaMiYira ;
    rdf:_2 pmc:KabbalahAshlagHakhraatAtzmoLeKhafZekhut ;
    rdf:_3 pmc:KabbalahAshlagHakhraatKolHaOlam ;
    pm:seriesStatement "Repentance from fear makes one intermediate, half liable and half acquitted; the one missing commandment, love, tips oneself to merit, which is the second and third measure of love; only tipping the whole world gives the fourth and eternal measure. Each step is defined by the scale the person holds at it." ;
    skos:note "The source names a consequence of skipping the last step, entered as pmc:KabbalahAshlagAhavaNitzhitPresupposesHakhraatHaOlam."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§116 (קטז), 121 (קכא), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagHakhraatAtzmoLeKhafZekhut a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Tipping oneself to the scale of merit"@en, "Sich selbst zur Waagschale des Verdienstes neigen"@de ;
    skos:definition "By the one missing commandment, love, reached through repentance from love, the whole pan full of debts, all sins and past sorrows, is turned into a pan of merits, so that one regrets not having suffered twice as much; the sages call this inversion tipping."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: הכרעה לכף זכות (hakhraah le-khaf zekhut)."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §116 (קטז), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §117
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagAlYaaminBeAtzmo a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Not to trust oneself until the day of death"@en, "Sich bis zum Tod nicht trauen"@de ;
    skos:definition "As long as one is intermediate he must not trust himself until his death nor lean on the Knower's testimony of secrets; even after tipping the whole world the warning holds."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:KabbalahAshlagHatzyoHayyavVeHatzyoZakkai ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: אל יאמין בעצמו (al yaamin be-atzmo)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§117 (קיז), 121 (קכא), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagHoteEhadYeabbedTovaHarbe a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "One sin loses all attainment"@en, "Eine Sünde verliert alle Erlangung"@de ;
    skos:definition "If the intermediate, or even one who tipped the world, stumbles in a single sin, all his wondrous attainment in Torah and disclosure of the Face is lost at once and he returns to concealment, losing even the merits of his later years."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: וחוטא אחד יאבד טובה הרבה."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that does not come about or is lost, and its cause. It names how pmc:KabbalahAshlagTeshuvaMiYira and pmc:KabbalahAshlagHakhraatKolHaOlam fails or is lost."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§117 (קיז), 121 (קכא), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §120
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagOlamNidonAharRubo a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The world and the individual judged by the majority"@en, "Welt und Einzelner nach der Mehrheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Adding the one commandment of love after repentance from fear makes one mostly meritorious and tips all, even a pan full of sins, to merit; so even the completely wicked, after repentance from love, count as completely righteous."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §120 (קכ), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §121
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagHakhraatKolHaOlam a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Tipping the whole world to merit"@en, "Die ganze Welt zum Verdienst neigen (ewige Liebe)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Rising through wondrous Torah attainments until one is shown how all people will finally reach repentance from love; knowing God's dealings with every creature as the Good One who benefits all, one reaches the fourth, eternal measure of love, counted as if they had already repented."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: הכרעת כל העולם לכף זכות; אהבה נצחית."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §121 (קכא), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §122
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagNehamatTzibbur a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Seeing the community's consolation"@en, "Den Trost der Gemeinde sehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "One who suffers with the community merits to see its consolation, i.e. to tip them to merit and witness their comfort."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: זוכה ורואה בנחמת צבור."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§122 (קכב), 128 (קכח), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagTzaarImHaTzibburNehamatTzibbur a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Suffering with the community yields seeing its consolation"@en, "Mitleiden ergibt Trost der Gemeinde"@de ;
    skos:definition "One who suffers with the community sees its consolation."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:KabbalahAshlagTzaarImHaTzibbur ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:KabbalahAshlagNehamatTzibbur ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §122 (קכב), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagRoeBeNehamatTzibbur a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sign: seeing the community's consolation"@en, "Den Trost der Gemeinde sehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The announced fruit of sharing the public's suffering is to see its comfort."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: the text announces it as the mark of completion."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §122 (קכב), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §124
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagShaloshMiddotBeKholAdam a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Three measures in every person"@en, "Drei Maße in jedem Menschen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Wicked, intermediate and righteous are not separate people but measures every person passes, named from the measure of his perception of providence; the wicked condemn themselves and the world, the intermediate hold two scales, the righteous justify providence."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: מידת רשעים / בינונים / צדיקים."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§124 (קכד), 129 (קכט), 130 (קל), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §125
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagAhavaNitzhitPresupposesHakhraatHaOlam a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Disclosure for the whole world before the fourth love"@en, "Enthüllung für die ganze Welt vor der vierten Liebe"@de ;
    skos:definition "The fourth measure of love cannot be attained unless one first attains the disclosure destined for the whole world, which gives the power to tip all to merit."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:KabbalahAshlagAhavaNitzhit ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:KabbalahAshlagHakhraatKolHaOlam ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Without first attaining the disclosure destined for the whole world, which gives the power to tip all to merit, the fourth measure of love cannot be attained." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§121 (קכא), 125 (קכה), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmp:KabbalahAshlagTzaarImHaTzibbur a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Grieving with the community as over oneself"@en, "Mit der Gemeinde leiden"@de ;
    skos:definition "There is no other device: one must always grieve over the trouble of the public exactly as over one's own, so that the debit pan of the whole world is ready within him; then, when he tips himself to merit, he can tip the whole world as well and become completely righteous."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: להצטער עצמו בצרת הצבור (le-hitztaer atzmo be-tzarat ha-tzibbur)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§122 (קכב), 125 (קכה), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagTzaarImHaTzibburHakhraatHaOlam a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Grieving with the community lets one tip the world"@en, "Mitleiden ermöglicht die Welt zu neigen"@de ;
    skos:definition "By grieving always with the public one holds the world's debit pan within, so that tipping oneself also tips the whole world and one becomes completely righteous."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:KabbalahAshlagTzaarImHaTzibbur ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:KabbalahAshlagHakhraatKolHaOlam ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §125 (קכה), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §126
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagAkholVeShatoBeTzaarHaTzibbur a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Rejoicing while the community suffers"@en, "Freude ohne Mitleiden"@de ;
    skos:definition "One who has reached repentance from fear and rejoices in his assured reward, eating and drinking while the public suffers, is rebuked: his errors will not be atoned till he dies."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:KabbalahAshlagTzaarImHaTzibbur ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §126 (קכו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagTzaddiqGamurPresupposesTzaarImHaTzibbur a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Grieving with the community before complete righteousness"@en, "Mitleiden vor vollständiger Gerechtigkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "One who does not grieve with the community cannot reach repentance from love; his errors have no atonement while alive, the completely righteous aspect is lost to him and he departs as merely intermediate, never becoming righteous."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:KabbalahAshlagTeshuvaMeAhava, pmc:KabbalahAshlagHakhraatKolHaOlam ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:KabbalahAshlagTzaarImHaTzibbur ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "One who does not grieve with the community has no atonement for his errors while alive, loses the aspect of the wholly righteous and departs from the world as an intermediate only." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§126 (קכו), 128 (קכח), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §127
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagMiddatReshaimEinLaHeleq a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The uncorrected years of concealment have no share after death"@en, "Die unberichtigten Jahre der Verhüllung haben keinen Anteil nach dem Tod"@de ;
    skos:definition "Repentance from fear does not mend the years spent under concealment, the measure of the wicked within a person; that measure has no portion after death, so it wants to live and rejoice here for ever, while the intermediate measure in the same person is glad at the approaching death and its reward; only repentance from love corrects it."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: מידת רשעים (middat reshaim)."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that does not come about or is lost, and its cause. It names how pmc:KabbalahAshlagTeshuvaMiYira fails or is lost."@en ;
    skos:note "Written by the integrator from the reconciliation (unmatched record of pass B at §127); the first pass held it only inside pmc:KabbalahAshlagHesterEhadLoNitqan."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §127 (קכז), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §128
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagNifterKeBeinoni a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Dying as an intermediate: the righteous lost"@en, "Stirbt als Mittlerer"@de ;
    skos:definition "The intermediate who did not share the public's pain still feels evils from providence from his past, cannot reach repentance from love, loses the completely righteous aspect and departs as intermediate only."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that does not come about or is lost, and its cause. It names how pmp:KabbalahAshlagTzaarImHaTzibbur fails or is lost."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §128 (קכח), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §129
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagDibburNegedHaHargasha a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Justifying with the mouth against what one feels counts for nothing"@en, "Worte gegen das Gefühl zählen nicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "The name wicked depends on the depth of feeling; speech or thought justifying providence counts for nothing when it contradicts what all one's limbs and senses feel."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:KabbalahAshlagKolAsherTimtzaYadkha ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §129 (קכט), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §132
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagOrHaBittahon a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The light of trust: the intermediate measure for the moment, under concealment"@en, "Zeitweiliges Mittelmaß in der Verhüllung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Even under hidden providence, by extra effort in believing in punishment and reward, a light of strong confidence in God appears and one reaches for the moment the intermediate degree of disclosure, though one cannot hold it permanently."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: אור של בטחון גדול (or shel bitachon gadol)."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §132 (קלב), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagHitamtzutOrHaBittahon a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Effort in faith reveals the light of trust"@en, "Glaubensanstrengung ergibt zeitweiliges Mittelmaß"@de ;
    skos:definition "Extra exertion in faith reveals a light of trust and the intermediate measure for that time."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:KabbalahAshlagHitamtzutBeEmunatSakharVeOnesh ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:KabbalahAshlagOrHaBittahon ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §132 (קלב), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmp:KabbalahAshlagHitamtzutBeEmunatSakharVeOnesh a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Extra effort in believing in reward and punishment under concealment"@en, "Verstärkte Anstrengung im Glauben an Lohn und Strafe"@de ;
    skos:definition "While still under hidden providence, strive hard in believing in punishment and reward, which reveals a light of great trust."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §132 (קלב), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagOrHaBittahonEinoQavua a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The measure reached under concealment does not last"@en, "Mittelmaß in der Verhüllung hält nicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "The flaw of the intermediate measure reached under concealment is that one cannot keep one's measures permanently."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that does not come about or is lost, and its cause. It names how pmp:KabbalahAshlagHitamtzutBeEmunatSakharVeOnesh fails or is lost."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §132 (קלב), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagBeinoniQavuaPresupposesTeshuvaMiYira a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Repentance from fear to keep the intermediate measure"@en, "Furchtumkehr für ein dauerhaftes Mittelmaß"@de ;
    skos:definition "The intermediate measure gained under concealment cannot be held permanently except through repentance from fear."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:KabbalahAshlagOrHaBittahon ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:KabbalahAshlagTeshuvaMiYira ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Without repentance from fear the intermediate measure reached under concealment cannot be held permanently." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §132 (קלב), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §133
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagHaShomrimAlHaPetah a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "The guards at the palace door"@en, "Die Wächter am Palasttor"@de ;
    skos:definition "In the parable, the king posts cunning guards to mislead all who approach his palace; many are turned back again and again until they tire of trying; only the mighty whose patience holds defeat them and open the door."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:KabbalahAshlagKolAsherTimtzaYadkha ;
    skos:note "Parable of the time of concealment."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §133 (קלג), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagIqarHaAvodaPresupposesTeshuvaMeAhava a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "The chief service begins after repentance from love"@en, "Der Hauptdienst beginnt nach der Umkehr aus Liebe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Choice ceases after revealed providence, yet the chief work in Torah with love and fear only begins after repentance from love."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:KabbalahAshlagSulamMutzavArtza ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:KabbalahAshlagTeshuvaMeAhava ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    skos:note "The text sets the order and says nothing of what follows from skipping it; hence prescribed order."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §133 (קלג), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagLoIbbereiAlmaElaLeTzaddiqeiGemirei a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Choice ends, the work begins: the world made only for the wholly righteous"@en, "Die Wahl endet, die Arbeit beginnt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Choice operates only in concealment, yet attaining disclosure does not end toil: the main proper service in love and fear starts then; creation exists solely for the completely righteous."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §133 (קלג), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagNilauMiLenasot a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Tiring of the attempts at the door"@en, "Ermüdung an der Pforte"@de ;
    skos:definition "In the parable most who approached returned the way they came, came back again over days and years until worn out to try further."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that does not come about or is lost, and its cause. It names how pmp:KabbalahAshlagKolAsherTimtzaYadkha fails or is lost."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §133 (קלג), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagSulamMutzavArtza a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Climbing the ladder of degrees after the disclosure"@en, "Aufstieg auf der Leiter nach der Enthüllung"@de ;
    skos:definition "After the door of revealed providence is opened, the chief service begins: the righteous ascend the numerous rungs of the ladder standing on earth whose top reaches heaven, going from strength to strength, each scorched by his fellow's canopy, until the thought of creation is fulfilled in them."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: סולם המוצב ארצה; מחיל אל חיל."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §133 (קלג), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §134
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagHaHesterSibatHaGiluy a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "No disclosure but where there was concealment"@en, "Keine Enthüllung ohne vorherige Verhüllung"@de ;
    skos:definition "A higher law: disclosure comes only where concealment was, as grain comes up solely at the spot where the seed was sown and decayed; concealment and disclosure relate like wick and flame, and the greater the hiding, the greater the light revealed once it is repaired."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: ההסתר הוא סיבת הגילוי."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§134 (קלד), 138 (קלח), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §135
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagKolHaToraShemotav a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The whole Torah is God's names"@en, "Die ganze Tora ist Gottes Namen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The sages say the whole Torah is names of God, though it includes the wicked, prohibitions and curses; this is explained by the garments of concealment that, once repaired, reveal the light."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §135 (קלה), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §136
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagLoDerakhavDerakheinu a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "His way runs from perfection downward, ours upward"@en, "Sein Weg abwärts, unserer aufwärts"@de ;
    skos:definition "Our way goes from imperfect to perfect; from God all disclosures come from complete perfection descending by contraction after contraction to our material world."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §136 (קלו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §137
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagToraDeAtzilut a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Torah of Atzilut and Torah of this world"@en, "Tora von Azilut und Tora dieser Welt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Torah was emanated as one with God (Torah of Atzilut), then descended through many contractions until given at Sinai in coarse garments; the Light inside is unchanged, and the coarse garments are more valuable at the end of their repair than the pure upper ones."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: תורה דאצילות; אורייתא וקוב\"ה חד הוא."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§137 (קלז), 138 (קלח), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §139
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagMosheVeHaMalakhim a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Moses and the angels"@en, "Mose und die Engel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Moses defeated the angels' claim to the Torah by showing that in their pure garments, without envy or evil inclination, the greatest lights cannot be revealed as through the garments of this world."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Moshe" ;
    pm:nameRole "the one who won the Torah from the angels by showing that the greatest lights appear only through the garments of this world" ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: משה; מלאכים."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §139 (קלט), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §140
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagMoreh a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "God called Teacher"@en, "Gott als Lehrer"@de ;
    skos:definition "God is called Moreh because He is clothed in the Torah; even under double hiding He dwells clothed in Torah, whose coarse garments are wings covering Him."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Moreh" ;
    pm:nameRole "God as clothed in the Torah, covered by its garments until the fourth degree" ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: מורה (moreh)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §140 (קמ), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagReiyatHaMoreh a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Seeing one’s Teacher: Torah and God one"@en, "Den Lehrer sehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "On reaching disclosure of the Face through love-repentance at its fourth level, the garments of Torah no longer cover the Teacher; it is revealed to one forever that Torah and God are one."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: והיו עיניך רואות את מוריך; אורייתא וקוב\"ה חד."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §140 (קמ), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagLoYikkanefOdMorekha a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sign: the garments of Torah no longer cover the Teacher"@en, "Gewänder der Tora verhüllen nicht mehr"@de ;
    skos:definition "At the fourth aspect, the Teacher is no longer hidden and one sees Him, knowing forever that Torah and God are one."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: the text announces it as the mark of completion."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §140 (קמ), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §141
#

pmp:KabbalahAshlagOtiAzavuVeToratiShamaru a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Seeking God in the Torah rather than by fasting"@en, "Gott in der Tora suchen statt im Fasten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Those who fasted and afflicted themselves to find God's face are told in His name that their toil is in vain, since He is found nowhere but in Torah: keep the Torah and search for Him there, and its Light will reform you."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:KabbalahAshlagMetzaarinNafshinVeLeitDeMashgah (Haqdama, §64): there those who afflict themselves and cry out are not heeded, for want of the inner Torah; here those who fast to find His face are told their toil is vain because He lets Himself be found nowhere outside the Torah, and its Light brings them back."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §141 (קמא), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagShmiratHaToraMetzia a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Keeping the Torah to seek Him brings the finding"@en, "Tora halten, um Gott zu suchen, bringt Finden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Keeping Torah and searching for God there, its Light reforms the seeker and he finds Him."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:KabbalahAshlagOtiAzavuVeToratiShamaru ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:KabbalahAshlagGiluyPanim ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §141 (קמא), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §142
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagDimyonotKozvim a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Against the false imaginings of the many about Kabbalah"@en, "Gegen falsche Vorstellungen von Kabbala"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author explains the essence of Kabbalah so the reader will not mislead himself with the false imaginings most of the masses hold."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:KabbalahAshlagEsekBeHokhmatHaQabbala ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §142 (קמב), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagOlamShanaNefesh a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Four aspects of Torah: world, year, soul, and their sustaining"@en, "Vier Aspekte der Tora: Welt, Jahr, Seele, Bestand"@de ;
    skos:definition "Torah divides into the outer reality (world), the inner reality of living beings (soul), the chain of causes through generations (year), and all the ways these are sustained and conducted."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: עולם, שנה, נפש; קיום המציאות."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §142 (קמב), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §144
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagHotamVeNehtamABYA a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The four worlds as seal and imprint"@en, "Vier Welten als Siegel und Abdruck"@de ;
    skos:definition "Atzilut, Beriah, Yetzirah and Asiyah issued one from another as seal and imprint, so all that is here derives from Atzilut, and every new thing must first appear there."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: חותם ונחתם."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:KabbalahAshlagHotamVeNehtam (Petiha, §115): there seal and imprint distinguish a partzuf from a world; here they say that all world, year and soul in this world, and every new thing, first appear in Atzilut and pass down."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §144 (קמד), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §146
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagQabbalaVeNigleHaynuHakh a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Kabbalah and revealed Torah: the same Torah"@en, "Kabbala und offenbare Tora sind dasselbe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Torah clothed in material world-year-soul is revealed Torah; clothed in the pure ones of the upper three worlds it is the wisdom of Kabbalah; the difference lies only in the person: two may study the same halakhah in the same words, and for one it is Kabbalah and Torah of Atzilut, for the other Torah of Asiyah."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§146 (קמו), 147 (קמז), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagToraDeYetziraVeAtzilut a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "One's Torah becoming the wisdom of Kabbalah"@en, "Die eigene Tora wird Kabbala"@de ;
    skos:definition "When one attains disclosure of the Face the revealed Torah's garments become refined for him, and his Torah turns into Torah of Yetzirah, called the wisdom of Kabbalah, and at higher attainment Torah of Atzilut, without any change of letters."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: תורה דיצירה; תורה דאצילות."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §146 (קמו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §148
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagPeshat a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Peshat: the Torah of Atzilut, stripped of garments"@en, "Peschat: die Tora von Azilut, von den Gewändern entkleidet"@de ;
    skos:definition "The end of the attainment of Torah: the plain sense, the Torah of Atzilut, so called because it is stripped of every garment that hides God."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: פשט (peshat)."@en ;
    skos:note "Member of a series written by the integrator."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §148 (קמח), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagRemez a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Remez: the Torah of Yetzira"@en, "Remes: die Tora von Jezira"@de ;
    skos:definition "The middle of the attainment of Torah: hint, the Torah of Yetzira, where He is more revealed."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: רמז (remez)."@en ;
    skos:note "Member of a series written by the integrator."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §148 (קמח), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagSod a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sod: the revealed Torah of Assiya, where He is hidden"@en, "Sod: die offenbare Tora von Assija, in der Er verborgen ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "The beginning of the attainment of Torah: the revealed Torah of Assiya, called secret because God hides in it entirely and its garments cover Him."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: סוד (sod)."@en ;
    skos:note "Member of a series written by the integrator."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §148 (קמח), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagSodRemezPeshat a pm:Sequencing ;
    rdfs:label "Sod, remez, peshat, after the Gra"@en, "Sod, Remes, Peschat"@de ;
    skos:definition "Torah begins in sod (revealed Torah of Asiyah where God hides), then remez (Torah of Yetzirah), ending in peshat (Torah of Atzilut, stripped of garments)."@en ;
    rdf:_1 pmc:KabbalahAshlagSod ;
    rdf:_2 pmc:KabbalahAshlagRemez ;
    rdf:_3 pmc:KabbalahAshlagPeshat ;
    pm:seriesStatement "After the Gra as the author reads him, the attainment of Torah begins in sod, the revealed Torah of Assiya where God is wholly hidden, passes through remez, the Torah of Yetzira where He is more revealed, and ends in peshat, the Torah of Atzilut stripped of every garment that covers Him." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §148 (קמח), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagToraDeAtzilutPresupposesSodVeRemez a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Sod and remez before peshat"@en, "Gra: Geheimnis, Andeutung, einfacher Sinn"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Gra writes Torah begins in sod (the revealed Torah of Asiyah where God is wholly hidden), then remez (Torah of Yetzirah), until one merits peshat, Torah of Atzilut, stripped of every garment hiding God."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:KabbalahAshlagToraDeYetziraVeAtzilut ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:KabbalahAshlagEsekBeHokhmatHaQabbala ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    skos:note "The text sets the order and says nothing of what follows from skipping it; hence prescribed order."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §148 (קמח), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §149
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagABYAKeNegedHashgahaVeAhava a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "The four holy worlds mapped to the ways of providence and the measures of love"@en, "Zuordnung der vier Welten"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author maps Asiyah to the two hidings (mostly evil, the little good mixed), Yetzirah to the first disclosure (half good half evil: the intermediate), Beriah to the second and third love (mostly good, the evil unnoticed), Atzilut to the fourth eternal love (no evil), using Etz Chayim gate 48."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Yehuda Leib Ashlag, in the Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot" ;
    dcterms:date "1956"^^xsd:gYear ;
    skos:note "The ordering is the author’s: he arranges the material he expounds; the date is the first year of the edition read (Jerusalem, 1956-1966)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:compilerInference ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§149 (קמט), 150 (קנ), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §151
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagABYADeQelippa a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The four worlds of the husks"@en, "Die vier Welten der Schalen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Opposite each holy world stands a world of the shells built from its lack: Asiyah of the shells rules through both hidings to tip all to guilt; Yetzirah of the shells holds the unrepaired debit pan and rules the intermediates; Beriah of the shells can cancel the thing on which love depends; Atzilut of the shells, set opposite Beriah, can trip the third love by providence over others; the holy Atzilut has no hold for them."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "ABYA di-qelippa" ;
    pm:nameRole "four impure worlds, each built from the lack of the holy world opposite it" ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: אבי\"ע דקליפה (ABYA de-kelippah)."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:KabbalahAshlagShteiMaarakhotABYA (Haqdama, §10): there two opposed systems are given the will to bestow and the will to receive; here each impure world is matched to a defect in the measure of love of the holy world opposite, and impure Atzilut stands against Beria, while holy Atzilut gives them no hold."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §§151 (קנא), 152 (קנב), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §154
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagSifreiQabbalaLeMasigim a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Books of Kabbalah written for those who attained"@en, "Kabbalabücher für Erlangende geschrieben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Most authors of Kabbalah books wrote for readers who have already reached disclosure of the Face and the upper attainments."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §154 (קנד), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagHavanatHaToraPresupposesOlamShanaNefesh a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Knowing world, year and soul above to understand their Torah"@en, "Kenntnis von Welt, Jahr und Seele"@de ;
    skos:definition "As one ignorant of this world's affairs would invert the revealed Torah, so one who has attained must still know all of world, year, soul in the upper worlds in detail to understand the Torah belonging to them."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:KabbalahAshlagToraDeYetziraVeAtzilut ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:KabbalahAshlagHagutBeSifreiHaQabbala ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Like one ignorant of this world who would turn the Torah’s matters from bad to good and good to bad, one who has attained but lacks knowledge of world, year and soul above cannot understand the Torah belonging to them." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §154 (קנד), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmp:KabbalahAshlagHagutBeSifreiHaQabbala a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Studying the books of Kabbalah even after attaining"@en, "Kabbalabücher auch nach der Erlangung studieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Even one who has attained, even from Torah of Atzilut, knows from it only what concerns his own soul; he must still know all of world, year and soul in the upper worlds, set out in the Zohar and true Kabbalah books, in which every wise man who understands on his own is obliged to meditate day and night."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §154 (קנד), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §155
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagOrotMaqifim a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Illumination from the surrounding lights"@en, "Erleuchtung durch die umgebenden Lichter"@de ;
    skos:definition "The lights destined for a person's soul stand ready as surrounding lights; while studying Kabbalah and naming lights and vessels that belong to his soul, these shine on him in some measure, from outside, drawing grace from above and abundance of holiness and purity that bring him much nearer to completion."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: אורות מקיפים (orot makifim)."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §155 (קנה), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmp:KabbalahAshlagLimudMitokhHaHesheq a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Studying Kabbalah with yearning even without understanding"@en, "Kabbala mit starkem Verlangen lernen, auch ohne Verständnis"@de ;
    skos:definition "Study Kabbalah with yearning and strong will to understand, even when one does not understand, uttering the names of lights and vessels belonging to one's soul; this is said to arouse the surrounding lights."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: מתוך החשק והרצון החזק להבין."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §155 (קנה), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagLimudMitokhHaHesheqOrotMaqifim a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Study with yearning awakens the surrounding lights"@en, "Kabbalastudium mit Verlangen ergibt umgebendes Licht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Studying with strong desire to understand, naming lights and vessels, awakens the surrounding lights which shine on the learner and bring him near to his completion."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:KabbalahAshlagLimudMitokhHaHesheq ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:KabbalahAshlagOrotMaqifim ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §155 (קנה), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagKolYisraelMuvtah a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Every one of Israel will finally attain all"@en, "Jeder Jude wird alles erlangen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Every person of Israel is assured to attain finally all the attainments in the thought of creation; one who does not in this incarnation will in another, as stated in the Zohar."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: גלגול (gilgul)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §155 (קנה), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# §156
#

pmp:KabbalahAshlagLoLehagshim a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Studying without materialising the matters"@en, "Lernen, ohne die Dinge zu verkörperlichen"@de ;
    skos:definition "While studying the wisdom, keep its matters from being turned into imagined and bodily things; the author made his commentaries on Ez Hayyim to save readers from every such materialising."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: שלא יגשימו הדברים (shello yagshimu ha-devarim)."@en ;
    skos:note "Written by the integrator as the prior step of the prerequisite at §156; the first pass named the condition only as a caution."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §156 (קנו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagOrotMaqifimPresupposesLoLehagshim a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Studying without materialising, or harm instead of benefit"@en, "Keine Verkörperlichung; vierzig Jahre oder ein Lehrer"@de ;
    skos:definition "The strict condition while studying is not to materialize the matters; otherwise one receives harm instead of benefit. Hence the sages warned not to study before forty or except from a teacher, as precaution."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:KabbalahAshlagOrotMaqifim ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:KabbalahAshlagLoLehagshim ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "One who materialises the matters receives harm instead of benefit." ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: לאחר ארבעים שנה (le-ahar arbaim shana)."@en ;
    skos:note "Hence, the text says, the sages warned not to study before forty or except from a teacher."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §156 (קנו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagTenaiHamur a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "The strict condition: not to materialise the matters"@en, "Strenge Bedingung: nicht verkörperlichen"@de ;
    skos:definition "While studying one must not materialize the matters into imagined or physical things, transgressing the ban on images; then one receives harm instead of benefit."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:KabbalahAshlagLimudMitokhHaHesheq, pmp:KabbalahAshlagEsekBeHokhmatHaQabbala ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §156 (קנו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagPanimMeirotKimatLeLoHoil a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The author's first commentary nearly in vain"@en, "Der erste Kommentar war fast nutzlos"@de ;
    skos:definition "After four parts of Panim Meirot u-Panim Masbirot were printed and spread, the author saw he had not fulfilled his duty of explanation and his great effort was nearly in vain, because readers did not drill each term and confused the matters by forgetting."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that does not come about or is lost, and its cause. It names how pmc:KabbalahAshlagPanimMeirotUPanimMasbirot fails or is lost."@en ;
    skos:note "A failure of the author's own earlier method, which he gives as the reason for the present work."@en ;
    skos:note "Failure of the author's own method, which motivates TES."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §156 (קנו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmp:KabbalahAshlagSheqidaAlPerushKolMila a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Diligence over the meaning of every word"@en, "Sorgfalt bei der Bedeutung jedes Begriffs"@de ;
    skos:definition "The reader must apply himself to the explanation of every word he meets and review it several times so as to remember it wherever it recurs, since in such fine matters one forgotten word blurs the whole subject."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §156 (קנו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagPerushHaMilot a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "The alphabetical explanation of terms (Perush ha-Milot)"@en, "Alphabetisches Begriffswörterbuch"@de ;
    skos:definition "To cure forgetting, the author began an alphabetical explanation of all Kabbalistic terms: on one side collecting the Ari's and early Kabbalists' explanations, on the other a distilled faithful definition usable wherever the term appears."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Yehuda Leib Ashlag, in the Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot" ;
    dcterms:date "1956"^^xsd:gYear ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: פירוש המלות (perush ha-milot)."@en ;
    skos:note "The ordering is the author’s: he arranges the material he expounds; the date is the first year of the edition read (Jerusalem, 1956-1966)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:compilerInference ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §156 (קנו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagTalmudEserHaSefirotMivne a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "The structure of Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot"@en, "Aufbau des Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author compiles the main passages on the ten sefirot from the Ari, chiefly Etz Chayim, at the head of each page, with two commentaries, Or Pnimi (explaining the Ari's words) and Histaklut Pnimit (the matter in its general scope), divided into sixteen parts each a lesson on one topic, with tables of questions and of answers on all terms and matters."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Yehuda Leib Ashlag, in the Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot" ;
    dcterms:date "1956"^^xsd:gYear ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: תלמוד עשר הספירות; אור פנימי; הסתכלות פנימית."@en ;
    skos:note "The ordering is the author’s: he arranges the material he expounds; the date is the first year of the edition read (Jerusalem, 1956-1966)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:compilerInference ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §156 (קנו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmp:KabbalahAshlagLuahHaSheelot a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Testing oneself with the tables of questions and answers"@en, "Selbstprüfung mit Fragen- und Antworttafeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "After finishing each part the student should try whether he can answer every question in the table, then check the matching answer; even if he knows them by memory he should repeat them very many times so he recalls a term, or at least its place, when needed."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: לוח השאלות / לוח התשובות."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §156 (קנו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagKeMunahimBeQufsa a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sign: every answer ready as if lying in a box"@en, "Jede Frage richtig beantworten"@de ;
    skos:definition "The student checks that he can answer every question properly against the answer table and drills until the answers lie ready as in a box."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: the text announces it as the mark of completion."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §156 (קנו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagSederHaLimudHavana a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "The order of study yields recall and understanding"@en, "Die Lernordnung ergibt Behalten und Verstehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Following the order and drilling is said to let the student remember each term when needed and understand the Pnim even without the commentary; may God's will succeed in his hand."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:KabbalahAshlagSederHaLimud ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:KabbalahAshlagHavanaBeTaamamUNimuqam ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §156 (קנו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmp:KabbalahAshlagSederHaLimud a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "The order of study of Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot"@en, "Lernordnung für Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot"@de ;
    skos:definition "Steps: (1) study the Pnim, the Ari's words at the head of the pages, to the end of the book, repeating several times even without understanding; (2) study the Or Pnimi commentary until one can understand the Pnim without its help; (3) study Histaklut Pnimit until understood and wholly remembered; (4) test oneself with the table of questions, then look at the answer marked with the same letter, for every question; (5) review and drill repeatedly until remembered as if lying in a box."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: סדר הלימוד (seder ha-limmud)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §156 (קנו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmp:KabbalahAshlagLimudHaPenim a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Studying the Pnim first, even without understanding"@en, "Zuerst den Pnim lernen, auch ohne Verständnis"@de ;
    skos:definition "First study the Pnim, the Ari's words printed at the head of the pages, to the end of the book, and repeat them several times even without understanding, after the rule that one first learns and then reasons."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: פנים (penim)."@en ;
    skos:note "Member of a series written by the integrator from the steps of pmp:KabbalahAshlagSederHaLimud."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §156 (קנו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmp:KabbalahAshlagLimudHistaklutPenimit a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Studying Histaklut Penimit until it is understood and remembered"@en, "Histaklut Pnimit lernen, bis sie verstanden und behalten ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Then study the commentary Histaklut Penimit until one understands it and remembers all of it."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: הסתכלות פנימית (histaklut penimit)."@en ;
    skos:note "Member of a series written by the integrator from the steps of pmp:KabbalahAshlagSederHaLimud."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §156 (קנו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmp:KabbalahAshlagLimudOrPenimi a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Studying Or Penimi until the Pnim stands without it"@en, "Or Pnimi lernen, bis der Pnim ohne ihn verstanden wird"@de ;
    skos:definition "Then study the commentary Or Penimi, striving until one can learn and understand the Pnim well without its help."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: אור פנימי (or penimi)."@en ;
    skos:note "Member of a series written by the integrator from the steps of pmp:KabbalahAshlagSederHaLimud."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §156 (קנו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagSederHaLimudShelavim a pm:Sequencing ;
    rdfs:label "The steps of the order of study"@en, "Lernordnung für TES"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Pnim, then Or Penimi, then Histaklut Penimit, then the tables of questions with the answers checked and drilled."@en ;
    rdf:_1 pmp:KabbalahAshlagLimudHaPenim ;
    rdf:_2 pmp:KabbalahAshlagLimudOrPenimi ;
    rdf:_3 pmp:KabbalahAshlagLimudHistaklutPenimit ;
    rdf:_4 pmp:KabbalahAshlagLuahHaSheelot ;
    pm:seriesStatement "The author orders the study: first the Pnim, the Ari's words, repeated even without understanding; then Or Penimi until the Pnim is understood without it; then Histaklut Penimit until understood and remembered; then the tables of questions and answers. Each commentary is studied for what the step before it left open." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §156 (קנו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagHavanatHaPenimBliBiur a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sign: understanding the Pnim without the commentary"@en, "Den Pnim ohne Kommentar verstehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "A stated aim of studying Or Pnimi: to be able to learn and understand the Ari's text well without its help."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: the text announces it as the mark of completion."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §156 (קנו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagHelekShlishiPresupposesZikhronHaRishonim a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "The first two parts remembered before the third"@en, "Behalten der ersten zwei Teile vor dem dritten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Every word of the third part requires full memory of the first two; otherwise the matter blurs or a mistaken sense is taken, one error drags ten after it, until full misunderstanding forces the student to abandon study."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:KabbalahAshlagSederHaLimud ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:KabbalahAshlagSederHaLimud ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "If anything of the first two parts is forgotten the matter blurs or a wrong sense is taken; one error brings ten, until the student must put the study aside entirely." ;
    skos:note "The text speaks of the parts of the book: every word of its third part needs the first two remembered."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §156 (קנו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagHaMeayenLoYargish a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "The reader does not feel what he forgot"@en, "Vergessen eines Begriffs bringt das Studium zum Scheitern"@de ;
    skos:definition "The worst is that the reader does not notice what he forgot: matters blur or he adopts a wrong sense, and one error pulls ten more."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:KabbalahAshlagSederHaLimud, pmp:KabbalahAshlagSheqidaAlPerushKolMila ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §156 (קנו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagTautAhatGoreretEser a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Confusion cascades until the study is abandoned"@en, "Verwirrung führt zum Abbruch"@de ;
    skos:definition "Forgetting leads to blurring or wrong interpretation; one error brings ten, until total misunderstanding forces the reader to put the study aside entirely."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that does not come about or is lost, and its cause. It names how pmp:KabbalahAshlagSederHaLimud fails or is lost."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Haqdama le-Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, §156 (קנו), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# Histaklut Penimit, ch. 1
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagEinLanuMilot a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Our words fail for spiritual matters"@en, "Gewöhnliche Wörter versagen bei Geistigem"@de ;
    skos:definition "All our vocabulary is drawn from imagined sense impressions; even a refined word such as 'lights' is borrowed from sunlight or felt contentment, so it cannot by itself convey anything true about divinity, which is abstract from time, place and motion."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: המלות (ha-milot); אורות (orot)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 1, para 1 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagMedumaUMushelet a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Kabbalistic words not to be taken in their sense meaning"@en, "Kabbalistische Wörter nicht sinnlich verstehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Warning that words like 'lights' are imagined and borrowed and will not give the inquirer anything true if read by their worldly sense."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:KabbalahAshlagEinLanuMilot ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: מדומה ומושאלת (meduma u-mushelet)."@en ;
    skos:note "The same paragraph states the aim of the commentary, that a novice can come near the wisdom free of any materialising or mistake."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 1, para 1 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagMilaAhatBiltiMutzlahat a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "One unfit word derails the reader"@en, "Ein unpassendes Wort verwirrt den Leser"@de ;
    skos:definition "Failure condition for written exposition of the wisdom: if the writer fails with even a single word not fit for its purpose, the student is at once confused and loses his grip on the whole subject."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: יתבלבל המעיין (yitbalbel ha-me'ayen)."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that does not come about or is lost, and its cause. It names how pmc:KabbalahAshlagSefatHaAnafim fails or is lost."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 1, para 1 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagSefatHaAnafim a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The language of the branches"@en, "Sprache der Zweige"@de ;
    skos:definition "Kabbalists are said to have adopted a special idiom: since every thing or conduct in this world descends from a root above, the names of worldly branches are used as pointers to their upper roots, so attainment can be passed on orally and in writing across generations."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: שפת הענפים (sefat ha-anafim)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 1, para 1 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagPeqihatEinayimBeMarotHaShamayim a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Eyes opened to the visions of heaven"@en, "Geöffnete Augen für die Gesichte des Himmels"@de ;
    skos:definition "An attainable state in which one has expert familiarity with how the branches of this world relate to the roots above them, so the words of Kabbalah are understood in their true sense; the sages are said to convey their attainment (hasagah) through such language."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: נפקחו עיניהם במראות השמים (nifkehu eineihem be-mar'ot ha-shamayim); השגה (hasagah)."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 1, para 1 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagBituyimMatmihim a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Strange expressions not to be rejected"@en, "Befremdliche Ausdrücke nicht verwerfen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The reader is reassured and warned not to be put off by surprising, even humanly alien expressions in Kabbalah books; they follow from the constraint of the language of branches."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:KabbalahAshlagSefatHaAnafim ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: ביטויים מתמיהים (bituyim mat'mihim)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 1, para 1 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagLoLehashmitAnafNahut a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "No lowly branch may be dropped or replaced"@en, "Keinen niedrigrangigen Begriff weglassen oder ersetzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Kabbalists cannot omit a branch because of its lowly rank, since no two branches relate to one root; losing the matter tied to that expression would cause great flaw and confusion across the whole wisdom."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:KabbalahAshlagSefatHaAnafim ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: פגם ובלבול (pegam u-vilbul)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 1, para 1 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagSharsheretAhatAruka a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Kabbalah as one long chain of cause and effect"@en, "Kabbala als eine durchgehende Kette von Ursache und Wirkung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Statement on the fixity of the method: no other wisdom is so interlinked by cause and effect from beginning to end; therefore there is no freedom to exchange its designations, and the exact branch pointing to its root must always be used and elaborated until a precise definition emerges."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: שרשרת אחת ארוכה (sharsheret ahat aruka)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 1, para 1 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagHavanatHaMilotPresupposesBeqiut a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Expertise in branch and root, or a sage to translate, before the words are understood"@en, "Kenntnis der Zweig-Wurzel-Beziehungen (oder ein übersetzender Weiser) vor dem Verständnis"@de ;
    skos:definition "Understanding the words requires either one's own familiarity with how branches relate to roots or receiving the explanation from an accomplished sage."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:KabbalahAshlagGishaLaHokhmaBliHagshama ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:KabbalahAshlagPeqihatEinayimBeMarotHaShamayim, pmp:KabbalahAshlagMiPiHakhamMuvhak ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Otherwise one is like the blind groping a wall and understands not one word in its true sense." ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: בקיאות (beki'ut)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 1, para 1 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagKeIvrimMegashshimQir a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Like the blind groping a wall"@en, "Wie Blinde an der Mauer tastend"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sign of failure: those not yet expert in branch-root relations do not understand even one word in its true meaning."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: כעורים מגששים קיר (ke-ivrim megashshim kir)."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that does not come about or is lost, and its cause. It names how pmc:KabbalahAshlagPeqihatEinayimBeMarotHaShamayim fails or is lost."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 1, para 1 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmp:KabbalahAshlagMiPiHakhamMuvhak a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Receiving the explanation from an accomplished sage"@en, "Die Erklärung von einem bewährten Weisen empfangen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Whoever lacks the expertise should receive the interpretation from a recognized sage willing to render it into everyday speech, acting as a translator from the language of branches into ordinary speech."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: מפי חכם מובהק (mi-pi hakham muvhak)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 1, para 1 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmp:KabbalahAshlagLimudEserHaSefirotBeTaharatan a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Studying the ten sefirot in their spiritual purity"@en, "Die zehn Sefirot durch diesen Kommentar in ihrer geistigen Reinheit studieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author states he took pains to set out the ten sefirot following the ARI's teaching, abstracted from all sensory notions, so that every novice can come near the wisdom; the reader is to study them in that abstract sense."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: עשר הספירות (eser ha-sefirot)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 1, para 1 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagGishaLaHokhmaBliHagshama a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Approaching the wisdom without materialising; a door to the rest"@en, "Zugang zur Weisheit ohne Verkörperlichung; Öffnung für den Rest der Weisheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Gainable ability: a beginner can come to the wisdom without stumbling into materializing error, and once the ten sefirot are understood, a door opens to observe and know how to understand the remaining matters of the wisdom."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: להסתכל ולדעת (lehistakel ve-lada'at)."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 1, para 1 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagEserHaSefirotGishaBliHagshama a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "The ten sefirot in their purity give access without error"@en, "Das Studium der Sefirot in Reinheit ermöglicht Zugang ohne Verkörperlichung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author's explanation of the ten sefirot is said to let beginners approach without error and opens the way to the rest."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:KabbalahAshlagLimudEserHaSefirotBeTaharatan ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:KabbalahAshlagGishaLaHokhmaBliHagshama ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 1, para 1 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagEhadYahidUMeyuhad a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "All is included in Him: One, Unique, Unified"@en, "Alles ist im Schöpfer enthalten; Einer, Einziger, Geeinter"@de ;
    skos:definition "No essence, sensed or intellected, is absent from the Creator, since a giver gives only what he has; concepts separate or opposite for us (wisdom and sweetness, actor and act, sweet and bitter) are in his simple light one without distinction. 'One' means single equivalence, 'Unique' that all that issues from him has a single form, 'Unified' that one power works all acts and they return into one form, namely to do good."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: אחד יחיד ומיוחד (ehad yahid u-meyuhad)."@en ;
    skos:note "The author reads the triad after Ramban on Sefer Yetzira 1:7 and adds Rambam's knower, known and knowledge being one."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 1, para 1 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagLavKolMohaSavilDa a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Not every mind can bear this"@en, "Nicht jeder Verstand kann dies fassen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The matter of the divine unity is said to be very subtle, and not every mind can hold it."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:KabbalahAshlagEhadYahidUMeyuhad ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: לאו כל מוחא סביל דא (lav kol moha sevil da)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 1, para 1 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagShteiHavhanotBaHashpaa a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Two discernments in the influx: before and after it is received"@en, "Zwei Unterscheidungen im göttlichen Einfluss"@de ;
    skos:definition "Like the manna, which each tasted as he wished, a spiritual thing is simple yet includes all forms; one must always distinguish the upper abundance before it reaches a receiver (still simple, inclusive light) and after, when it takes one partial, separate form according to the receiver's nature."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: ב' הבחנות בהשפעה (shtei havhanot ba-hashpa'ah)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 1, para 2 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagOrEinSof a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The light of Ein Sof, not the Essence"@en, "Ein Sof (das Unendliche)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Held to be not the Essence but the light extending from it before the restriction, filling all reality without limit or end; the name belongs to that light. Later identified with the Thought of Creation, and as including all reality until the final correction."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Or Ein Sof barukh hu" ;
    pm:nameRole "the light extending from His essence before the restriction, called the Thought of Creation" ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: אור אין סוף (or Ein Sof)."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:KabbalahAshlagEinSof (Haqdama, §13): there Ein Sof is named as the seat of the Thought of Creation; here the name is said to belong not to the Essence but to the light extending from it, which leaves the Essence by the will to receive included in it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 1, para 5 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagShteiHavhanotBaMetziut a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "All reality before and after the restriction"@en, "Zwei Unterscheidungen der Wirklichkeit: vor und nach der Einschränkung"@de ;
    skos:definition "All worlds are viewed in two states: the form before the restriction, without bound or end, called Ein Sof; and from the restriction downward, in limit and measure, called the four worlds Atzilut, Beriah, Yetzirah, Assiyah."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: ד' העולמות אבי\"ע."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 1, para 5 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagAtzmuto a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The Creator's Essence"@en, "Das Wesen des Schöpfers (Atzmuto)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Held to be utterly beyond thought and without any name or epithet, since a name means attainment; all names apply only to the light extending from it."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "atzmuto yitbarakh" ;
    pm:nameRole "the essence, beyond all thought and without any name" ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: עצמותו (atzmuto)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 1, para 5 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagEinShemBeAtzmuto a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "No name for the Essence"@en, "Das Wesen nicht benennen oder bestimmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "What is not attained cannot be defined by a name; all names and epithets are to be referred only to the extended light, never to the Essence."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:KabbalahAshlagAtzmuto ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: שם וכינוי (shem ve-khinuy)."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:KabbalahAshlagHaqiraBeMaasavLoBeAtzmuto (Haqdama, §2): there inquiry into the Essence is barred; here naming it is, since every name means attainment, and all names belong to the extended light."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 1, para 5 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagBahitLeIstakkulei a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Bread of shame: why a world of labour"@en, "Brot der Scham: warum eine Welt der Mühe"@de ;
    skos:definition "The sages are cited: whoever eats what is not his is ashamed to look at the giver's face; every free gift carries the flaw of shame, so the Creator made this world with labor so souls later enjoy the fruit of their own toil as earned wages and are spared that shame. The author later re-reads this as pointing to how the receiving will differs in form from its root."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: בהית לאסתכולי באפיה (bahit le-istakulei be-apeih); מתנת חנם (matnat hinam)."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:KabbalahAshlagBushaMonaatQabbala (Petiha, §15): there shame keeps the guest from eating; here the sages' saying explains why this world of labour was made, and the author reads it as the will to receive differing in form from its root."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 1, para 6; ch. 4, para 5 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagSakharShivimShana a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against the plain reading of the sages' answer"@en, "Gegen die wörtliche Lesart der Antwort der Weisen über das Brot der Scham"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author argues the sages' answer is very difficult if taken literally: seventy years of labor in a passing world bear no proportion to eternal reward (310 worlds per righteous person), so the reward would still be a free gift; and he rejects the alternative that part is wage and part gift, since shame would remain. He concludes a deep intention lies behind their words."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: אין דבריהם אלו מובנים כפשוטם."@en ;
    skos:note "Entered as a concept: the author raises against the plain sense of the sages' answer that seventy years bear no proportion to eternal reward, so the reward would still be a free gift, and resolves it himself at ch. 4, para 5."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:firstPersonReport ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 1, para 7 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagOtzarMatnatHinnam a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The treasury of free gifts"@en, "Empfangen aus dem Schatz der freien Gaben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Cited as the chief aim of our prayer; the sages are said to hold this treasury ready solely for the very highest souls."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: אוצר מתנת חנם (otzar matnat hinam)."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 1, para 7 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagMahshavaAhat a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "One thought is actor, act, labour and reward"@en, "Ein einziger Gedanke ist Täter, Tat, Mühe und Lohn"@de ;
    skos:definition "Since the Creator is One, Unique and Unified, his works do not proceed by many thoughts; all reality, upper and lower, up to the final correction came forth from one thought, which is the actor, the substance of all acts, the receiver of the purpose, the essence of the labor, and itself the hoped-for perfection and reward."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: מחשבה אחת (mahshavah ahat)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 1, para 8 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagLoShteiMahshavot a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Not to think of two divine thoughts"@en, "Nicht sagen oder denken, es gebe zwei getrennte göttliche Gedanken"@de ;
    skos:definition "Doctrinal warning: spoilage and darkness, though opposite to the Creator, must be held to come from him within the single thought; it is forbidden even to think they stem from a second thought."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:KabbalahAshlagMahshavaAhat ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: ח\"ו לומר ולהרהר (has ve-shalom lomar u-le-harher)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 1, para 9 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# Histaklut Penimit, ch. 2
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagRatzonLeQabbelMaqom a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The will to receive as vessel and place"@en, "Der Wille zu empfangen als Gefäß und 'Ort'"@de ;
    skos:definition "From the Emanator's will to bestow there was necessarily stamped into the extending light a will to receive its pleasure; this will equals the light's entire size, exactly and is called 'place': as a person's capacity for bread depends on appetite, not stomach, in spirit the desire for abundance is its place and sets the abundance's measure."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: הרצון לקבל (ha-ratzon le-kabbel); מקום (makom)."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:KabbalahAshlagRatzonLeQabbel (Petiha, §1): the Petiha states that pleasure is measured by the will; here the will is named the abundance's place, after the measure of bread a man can eat, which depends on appetite and not on the stomach."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 2, para 2 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagRatzonMotziEinSofMeAtzmuto a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The will to receive takes Ein Sof out of the Essence"@en, "Der Wille zu empfangen hebt Ein Sof aus dem Wesen heraus"@de ;
    skos:definition "The light is named Ein Sof, rather than being nameless Essence, because it contains the will to receive, a new form not included in the Essence, since from whom would it receive; but before the restriction this new form was not discerned as different from the light: the saying that he and his name were one alone (Pirkei de-Rabbi Eliezer), where 'his name' is the place, Malkhut of Ein Sof."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: הוא ושמו אחד (hu u-shemo ehad)."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:KabbalahAshlagHuUShmoEhad (Haqdama, §13): there He and His Name being one says that the souls were in equivalence of form in the Infinite; here His Name is the place, the will to receive within the light, which before the restriction showed no difference from the light."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 2, paras 3, 4 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagMalkhutDeEinSof a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Malkhut of Ein Sof"@en, "Malkhut des Ein Sof"@de ;
    skos:definition "Held to be the receiving will held within Ein Sof's light, the Thought of Creation including all reality, and the totality of the receivers there; it made no end or limit on the light there, since no disparity of form had yet appeared."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Malkhut de-Ein Sof" ;
    pm:nameRole "the will to receive held in Ein Sof's light, the sum of all receivers, which sets no end there" ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: מלכות דאין סוף (malkhut de-Ein Sof)."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:KabbalahAshlagShemoRatzon (Petiha, §17): there Malkhut within the upper light is called His Name; here Malkhut of Ein Sof is also the Thought of Creation holding all reality and the totality of the receivers."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 2, para 5; ch. 6, para 3 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagTzimtzumMalkhutDeEinSof a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The restriction: Malkhut of Ein Sof lessens its will"@en, "Die Einschränkung (Zimzum)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Malkhut of Ein Sof adorned itself to rise and equalize its form more with the Essence, so it diminished its will to receive in the fourth phase, intending that the worlds unfold down to this world, where receiving would be repaired into the form of bestowal and reach equivalence with the Emanator; once the desire was reduced the light departed, since light depends on desire and there is no coercion in spirit."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: צמצום (tzimtzum); אין כפיה ברוחניות."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:KabbalahAshlagTzimtzumAlef (Petiha, §14): there the restriction separates phase four to save the creatures from separation; here Malkhut of Ein Sof adorns itself to equal the Essence in form and lessens its will, so that the light departs, since light depends on the will and there is no coercion in the spiritual."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 2, para 5 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# Histaklut Penimit, ch. 4
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagOrHozerBeQedushaRatzonBeTumaa a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Holy worlds receive with reflected light, impure ones with the restricted will"@en, "Zurückgeworfenes Licht als Gefäß; heilige gegenüber unreinen Welten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Following the tzimtzum and the masakh, the will to receive was disqualified as a vessel and left the holy system; reflected light was set in its place as the receiving vessel. This is said to be the whole difference between the holy and the impure worlds of ABYA: the holy receive with reflected light corrected to match Ein Sof in form, the impure use the restricted will to receive, opposite to Ein Sof, and are thereby severed from the source of all life."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: אור חוזר (or hozer); מסך (masakh)."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:KabbalahAshlagOrHozerKliQabbala (Petiha, §14): there reflected light becomes the vessel in place of phase four; here this is said to be the whole difference between the holy and the impure ABYA, the impure ones using the restricted will itself and so severed from the source of all life."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 4, para 1 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagShimreiHaQelippot a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The body nourished by the dregs of the husks"@en, "Der von den Hefen der Schalen genährte Körper"@de ;
    skos:definition "Default failure condition of the human: because the body draws its nourishment from youth from the dregs of the shells, it uses the will only to receive, its desire ever open to swallow the world; it is thereby cut off from life and full of filth, and the heart's inclination is evil from youth."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: שמרי הקליפות (shimrei ha-kelipot)."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that does not come about or is lost, and its cause. It names how pmc:KabbalahAshlagDevekutHashvaatHaTzura fails or is lost."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 4, para 2 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagLoNehenetiAfiluBeEtzbaQetana a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sign: not enjoying even with the little finger"@en, "Nicht einmal mit dem kleinen Finger genießen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced sign of the inverted vessel, exemplified by Rabbenu ha-Kadosh: no self-directed enjoyment at all while receiving."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: the text announces it as the mark of completion."@en ;
    skos:note "The exemplar is Rabbenu ha-Kadosh (Ketubot 104a)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 4, para 2 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagShutafutImHaBore a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Partnership with the Creator in completing creation"@en, "Partnerschaft mit dem Schöpfer bei der Vollendung der Schöpfung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Status gained by the righteous: completing the creation the Creator began."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: עמי אתם בשותפות."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 4, para 2 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagHipukhHaKelimShutafut a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Turning the vessels makes one a partner in creation"@en, "Gefäßumkehr macht zum Partner der Schöpfung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Because they turn receiving vessels into bestowing ones the righteous are said to complete creation as partners."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:KabbalahAshlagTorahUMitzvotAlMenatLeHashpia ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:KabbalahAshlagShutafutImHaBore ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 4, para 2 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagVeRagleihaYordotMavet a pm:Sequencing ;
    rdfs:label "From the will to enjoy down to death: 'her feet go down to death'"@en, "Abstieg vom Willen zu genießen bis zum Tod"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ordered stages named by the source: the will to enjoy first only dimmer than the light (darkness), then the kelipot and sitra ahra issue from it, then the wicked fed by them, cut off from the root of life, so that her feet go down to death."@en ;
    rdf:_1 pmc:KabbalahAshlagYeshMeAyin ;
    rdf:_2 pmc:KabbalahAshlagQelippot ;
    rdf:_3 pmc:KabbalahAshlagMetimBeHayeihem ;
    pm:seriesStatement "The will to enjoy is at first only dimmer than the light and so called darkness; at the end of the chain the husks and the Other Side issue from it, and from them death for the wicked who are fed by them; the verse of the feet that go down to death names the last place." ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: ורגליה יורדות מות (ve-ragleha yordot mavet)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 4, para 3 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagAnafVeShoresh a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The branch follows its root: pleasure and pain"@en, "Der Zweig folgt der Wurzel: Lust und Schmerz"@de ;
    skos:definition "Law that every branch's nature equals its root: what is in the root the branch loves and craves, what is not it hates and cannot bear. Since the Creator is root of all, what comes from him directly is pleasant (rest, wisdom, strength, wealth), and what is not in him and comes only via the axis of creation itself is against our nature and hard to bear (motion, folly, weakness, poverty, disgrace); we move only to attain rest because our root is without motion."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: ענף ושורש (anaf ve-shoresh); מנוחה (menuhah)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 4, para 4 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagMashalHaAshir a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The rich man’s parable: shame arises in the receiver"@en, "Scham und Ungeduld entstehen im Empfänger, mittelbar"@de ;
    skos:definition "Parable of a rich man who daily feeds and enriches a man from the market with ever larger gifts: the guest tastes great pleasure, which comes straight from the giver, and also shame and impatience at the free gifts, which arise from the receiver's own nature and are caused by the giver only indirectly. So the will to enjoy is no defect in the Creator's view but the very axis of creation; only the receiver bearing it feels it as hard to bear, because this form is absent from his root."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: קושי הסבלנות (koshi ha-savlanut); בושה (bushah)."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:KabbalahAshlagMashalBaalHaBayitVeOreah (Petiha, §15): there the guest's refusal becomes the vessel; here a rich man feeds a man from the market with growing gifts, and the shame he feels comes from the receiver's own nature, from the giver only indirectly."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 4, paras 4, 5 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagShuvEinaBahit a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sign: no longer ashamed to look at the Giver"@en, "Keine Scham mehr; die Vollkommenheit des Geschöpfs offenbart"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced result: once the soul is clean of the will to receive for itself it is no longer ashamed to look at the giver's face, and the final perfection of the creature is thereby revealed."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: שוב אינה בהית לאסתכולי באפיה."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: the text announces it as the mark of completion."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 4, para 5 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagHipukhHaKelimPresupposesGuf a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "The soul in a body in this world before the inversion of form"@en, "Verkörperung in dieser Welt vor der Formumkehr"@de ;
    skos:definition "The soul must come into this world and be clothed in a body; the great work of turning receiving into bestowing is said to be conceivable only here (the necessity of the far descent to be explained later)."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:KabbalahAshlagQabbalaAlMenatLeHashpia ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:KabbalahAshlagYeridatHaNefeshLaGuf ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "The inversion of receiving into bestowal is not conceivable anywhere but in this world." ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: מתלבשת בגוף (mitlabeshet be-guf)."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:KabbalahAshlagGmarHaRatzonPresupposesYeridaBaOlamot (Petiha, §3): there the will must descend through the four worlds to reach its final quality; here the soul must be clothed in a body in this world because only here can receiving be turned into bestowal."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 4, para 5 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagMishnehShibbaron a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The wicked broken twice over"@en, "Die Frevler erleiden doppelten Bruch"@de ;
    skos:definition "Failure sign: this world is made empty of good, possessions need motion, and motion pains as it is not directly from the Creator; yet staying empty is also against the root. Because all their gains are for themselves, and owning one hundred, one craves double, no one dies with half his craving fulfilled; they suffer both the pain of much motion and the pain of lacking half."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: משנה שברון שברם (mishneh shibbaron shovrem)."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a failure condition: the text names an outcome that does not come about or is lost, and its cause. It names how pmc:KabbalahAshlagSodHaMenuha fails or is lost."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 4, para 6 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagTzaddiqimYirshuMishneh a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sign: the righteous inherit double"@en, "Die Gerechten erben doppelt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Announced sign of success: after turning their will to receive into will to bestow, the righteous attain the perfection of pleasure and the best possessions, and also likeness of form to their Maker, true adhesion, and rest, the abundance coming to them by itself without motion or toil."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: בארצם ירשו משנה (be-artzam mishneh yirashu)."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: the text announces it as the mark of completion."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 4, para 6 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagHipukhHaRatzonMenuha a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "The turned will yields the double inheritance and rest"@en, "Umgekehrter Wille ergibt doppeltes Erbe und Ruhe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Receiving in order to bestow is said to yield both pleasure and possessions, and equivalence with rest."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:KabbalahAshlagTorahUMitzvotAlMenatLeHashpia ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:KabbalahAshlagSodHaMenuha ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 4, para 6 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagSodHaMenuha a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Rest: the abundance coming without motion"@en, "Ruhe: Fülle, die ohne Mühe kommt"@de ;
    skos:definition "State said to be attained with the double inheritance: being in the secret of rest, where the abundance reaches one by itself without any motion and labor."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: סוד המנוחה (sod ha-menuhah)."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 4, para 6 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# Histaklut Penimit, ch. 5
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagHaPoel a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The actor: thought becomes law in the created"@en, "Täter: der Gedanke als Gesetz im Geschaffenen"@de ;
    skos:definition "In the series of the single thought, 'the actor': what is only thought for the Creator becomes a binding law in creatures; since he thought to delight us, we are necessarily made receivers of his good."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: הפועל (ha-po'el)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 5, para 1 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagMahshavaAhatPoelPeulaYegiaSakhar a pm:Sequencing ;
    rdfs:label "The one thought as actor, action, labour and reward"@en, "Der einzige Gedanke als Täter, Tat, Mühe, Lohn"@de ;
    skos:definition "The source orders the aspects of the Thought of Creation in sequence, each taking its sense from its place: actor, action, labor and service, awaited reward."@en ;
    rdf:_1 pmc:KabbalahAshlagHaPoel ;
    rdf:_2 pmc:KabbalahAshlagHaPeula ;
    rdf:_3 pmc:KabbalahAshlagHaYegia ;
    rdf:_4 pmc:KabbalahAshlagHaSakhar ;
    pm:seriesStatement "The one Thought of Creation is in turn the actor, the action, the labour and the reward: what is only thought in Him becomes a binding law in us; that law makes us an act and not the actor; the craving grows through the worlds into a separate body, which is the labour; and the turning of the vessels by that labour is the whole reward." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 5, para 1 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagHaPeula a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The action: we are an act by the will to receive"@en, "Tat: wir sind als 'Tat' durch den Willen zu empfangen bestimmt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Second member: once the will to receive is stamped in us we are defined as an action, leaving the Creator's domain for that of the created."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: הפעולה (ha-pe'ulah)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 5, para 1 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagHaYegia a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The labour: the craving grown into a separate body"@en, "Mühe: das wachsende Verlangen bis zum getrennten Körper"@de ;
    skos:definition "Third member: the amount of craving grows through the chain of worlds until a separate earthly body, formally opposite to the source of life and unable to give outside itself, which brings death and all sufferings to the soul; that is the service of God in Torah and commandments."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: היגיעה והעבודה (ha-yegi'ah ve-ha-avodah)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 5, para 1 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagHaSakhar a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The reward: vessels corrected and fit for endless abundance"@en, "Lohn: berichtigte Gefäße, fähig zu endloser Fülle"@de ;
    skos:definition "Fourth member: by labor in Torah and commandments to bestow, the receiving vessels are slowly inverted; that is the whole awaited reward."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: השכר המקווה (ha-sakhar ha-mekuveh)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 5, para 1 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagQabbalatHaShefaPresupposesTiqqunHaKelim a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Corrected vessels before the mouth is opened wide"@en, "Berichtigte Gefäße vor dem Öffnen zum Empfang"@de ;
    skos:definition "As long as the receiving vessels are not corrected one cannot open one's mouth wide to receive the abundance, because of fear of the disparity of form (shame); the first tzimtzum happened on this account."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:KabbalahAshlagShefaAdEinQetz ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:KabbalahAshlagQabbalaAlMenatLeHashpia ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "As long as the vessels of receiving are uncorrected one cannot open one’s mouth wide for His abundance, for fear of the disparity of form." ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: להרחיב פינו (leharhiv pinu)."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:KabbalahAshlagTakhlitHaBeriaPresupposesHizdakkekhut (Petiha, §12): there refining the will is commanded or the aim is not reached; here the uncorrected vessel cannot receive because of the shame of disparity, and the first restriction itself came about on this account."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 5, para 1 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagTiqqunHaKelimShefaAdEinQetz a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Labour to bestow makes one fit for endless abundance"@en, "Mühe um zu geben ergibt Eignung für endlose Fülle"@de ;
    skos:definition "Correction of the vessels through Torah and commandments with intent to bestow is said to make one fit to receive without limit."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:KabbalahAshlagTorahUMitzvotAlMenatLeHashpia ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:KabbalahAshlagShefaAdEinQetz ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 5, para 1 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagShefaAdEinQetz a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Fit to receive His abundance without end"@en, "Eignung, Fülle ohne Ende zu empfangen"@de ;
    skos:definition "When the receiving vessels are corrected to be for bestowal they equal their Maker and become worthy to receive his abundance endlessly."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: שפעו עד אין קץ (shif'o ad ein ketz)."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 5, para 1 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagMalkhutDeEinSofEinaOsaSof a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Malkhut of Ein Sof makes no end"@en, "Malkhut des Ein Sof setzt kein Ende"@de ;
    skos:definition "Answering the Tikkunei Zohar, the will to receive in Ein Sof is called its Malkhut, but there it set no end or boundary to the light since no disparity of form was revealed; hence 'Ein Sof' (no end); after the restriction Malkhut makes an end in every sefirah and partzuf."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: סוף (sof); גבול (gevul)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 5, para 2 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagNirashuHaSippim a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against those who object to a Malkhut in Ein Sof"@en, "Gegen die Einwände gegen eine Malkhut im Ein Sof"@de ;
    skos:definition "Citing the Tikkunei Zohar, the author notes the thresholds shook from the voice of objectors asking how Malkhut can be named in Ein Sof, implying nine prior sefirot there; he answers that it is the will to receive which made no limit there."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: נרעשו הספים (nir'ashu ha-sippim)."@en ;
    skos:note "A dispute entered as a concept: the opposing view is reported by the author and not read in a work of its own."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 5, para 2 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# Histaklut Penimit, ch. 6
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagHitorerutMiKoahAtzmo a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The vessel fixed only by the emanated's own arousal"@en, "Das Gefäß muss durch eigene Erweckung des Emanierten offenbar werden"@de ;
    skos:definition "The vessel, root of darkness, is wrought gradually by cause and effect like pregnancy and birth ('the waters conceived and bore darkness'); the will included from the Emanator's side is not enough: the emanated itself must draw more abundance than the extension gave, and only then are craving and desire fixed so the light can be clothed in it permanently. In Ein Sof this occurred through all four phases without any discerned change."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: התעוררות מכח עצמו (hit'orerut mi-koah atzmo)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 6, para 2 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# Histaklut Penimit, ch. 7
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagRuhaniEinoNehlaq a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The spiritual does not divide: the light left all four phases"@en, "Geistige Unteilbarkeit: das Licht verließ alle vier Phasen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The middle point, the will to enjoy, felt receiving as an indirect drawing (as in the rich-man parable) and reduced its desire from the last phase to add adhesion; though only the fourth phase was reduced, the light emptied the whole place, because the spiritual does not divide into parts."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: אינו נחלק לחלקים (eino nehlak la-halakim)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 7, para 1 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagMiluiTzimtzumQav a pm:Sequencing ;
    rdfs:label "Filling, restriction, line"@en, "Erfüllung, Einschränkung, Linie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Stages ordered in the source: Ein Sof light fills all reality; the restriction empties the place; the line is drawn back into three phases leaving the fourth vacant."@en ;
    rdf:_1 pmc:KabbalahAshlagOrEinSof ;
    rdf:_2 pmc:KabbalahAshlagTzimtzumMalkhutDeEinSof ;
    rdf:_3 pmc:KabbalahAshlagRuhaniEinoNehlaq ;
    rdf:_4 pmc:KabbalahAshlagQavVeHalalPanui ;
    pm:seriesStatement "First the light of Ein Sof fills all reality; then Malkhut of Ein Sof lessens its will and the light leaves the whole place, though only the fourth phase was lessened; then a line of light is drawn back into the first three phases and the fourth remains a vacant space. Each stage is read from the one before it." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 7, para 2 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagQavVeHalalPanui a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The line and the vacant space"@en, "Die Linie und der leere Raum"@de ;
    skos:definition "Afterwards the Ein Sof light was drawn again into the emptied place as a line filling only the first three phases, as the restricted point wished; the fourth remained hollow. Since the phases are mutually included, within the fourth too the light reached its first three, and only the last of the fourth remained empty."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: קו (kav); חלל פנוי (halal panui)."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:KabbalahAshlagQavDaq (Petiha, §31): there Adam Kadmon is a thin line in the vacant space relative to the Infinite; here the line is the light of Ein Sof drawn back into the first three phases, leaving only the last of the fourth empty."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 7, para 2 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# Histaklut Penimit, ch. 8
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagHokhmaOrHasadimMayim a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Wisdom called light, mercies called water"@en, "Weisheit heißt Licht, Gnaden heißen Wasser"@de ;
    skos:definition "In Atzilut two kinds of light: Hokhmah, called light, drawn from above without help from below; Hasadim, called water, drawn with the lower's help, as light's nature is rooted above and water's below. Upper waters come through the second phase (Binah), lower waters through the fourth (Malkhut)."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: אור (or); מים (mayim); מים עליונים ומים תחתונים."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:KabbalahAshlagOrHasadimDevekut (Petiha, §5): there Hasadim is the light drawn by adhesion; here it is called water because it is drawn with the lower's help, and Bina and Malkhut are the upper and the lower waters."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 8, para 1 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagBinaHitgabbrutHaRatzon a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Bina: Hokhma that strengthened its will"@en, "Bina (zweite Phase)"@de ;
    skos:definition "Held to be the part of Hokhmah that intensified its desire and drew more than its extension, thereby slightly thickening and acquiring disparity of form; the added abundance is light of Hasadim or upper waters; it contains three lights and is only root and actor of the vessel; first heh."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: בינה (binah)."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:KabbalahAshlagBehinaBetBina (Petiha, §5): there Bina arises from a desire to bestow; here Bina is the part of Hokhma that strengthened its will and drew more than its extension, thickening a little, and the added abundance is Hasadim."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 8, para 2 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagOtiyotHavayaKelim a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "The letters of the Name as grades of the vessel"@en, "Sefirot den Buchstaben und ihren Formen zugeordnet"@de ;
    skos:definition "Systematization by the author: the letters indicate not the quantity of light but the grades of the vessel's formation (white of the Torah scroll's parchment is light, black letters vessels); hence Keter only a tip, Hokhmah the smallest letter with a short leg (potential not yet actual), Binah the broad heh, Zeir Anpin the long thin vav (vessel still hidden, revealed at its end), Malkhut a heh like Binah since in Tikkun they resemble and lend each other vessels."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Yehuda Leib Ashlag, in the Histaklut Penimit to Part 1 of Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot" ;
    dcterms:date "1956"^^xsd:gYear ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: קוצו של יוד (kotzo shel yod)."@en ;
    skos:note "The ordering is the author’s: he arranges the material he expounds; the date is the first year of the edition read (Jerusalem, 1956-1966)."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:KabbalahAshlagArbaOtiyotHavaya (Petiha, §3): there the four phases match the four letters; here the shapes of the letters are read: black letters as vessels on the white of the parchment as light, Keter only the tip of the yod, the small yod with its short leg, the broad he, the long thin vav, and the last he like the first because Bina and Malkhut lend each other vessels."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:compilerInference ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 8, para 4 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# Histaklut Penimit, ch. 9
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagTenuaRuhanit a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Spiritual motion is renewal of form"@en, "Geistige Bewegung ist Erneuerung der Form"@de ;
    skos:definition "Motion in this wisdom is not change of place but every new form; the new form, differing from the prior general form, counts as having separated and moved off with its own name and rule, like a part detached from a body moving away."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: תנועה (tenu'ah); חידוש צורה."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:KabbalahAshlagAliyotVeYeridotEinamMaqom (Petiha, §11): there rising and falling are warned against as spatial; here every motion in the wisdom is defined as a new form that separates and goes out under its own name."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 9, para 1 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagZmanRuhani a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Spiritual time: a number of linked renewals"@en, "Geistige Zeit ist eine Zahl verketteter Veränderungen; vorher und nachher heißt Ursache und Wirkung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Our notion of time is only the feeling of motions, which imagination arranges in sequence; in total rest there would be no time. Likewise in spirit a sum of form-renewals linked as cause and effect is called time, and 'before and after' always means cause and effect."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: זמן (zman); קודם ואח\"כ."@en ;
    skos:note "Differs from pmc:KabbalahAshlagQodemVeAharSibaVeMesovav (Petiha, §58): there the reader is warned that before and after mean cause and effect; here time itself is defined as the feeling of motions, and in the spiritual as a sum of renewals of form linked as cause and effect."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 9, para 2 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .


#
# Histaklut Penimit, ch. 10
#

pmc:KabbalahAshlagTzuraRishonaHomer a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The first form called matter, since essence is not grasped"@en, "Die erste Form heißt Materie, weil das Wesen nicht erfasst wird"@de ;
    skos:definition "Though the will to receive seems a mere accident or form, we name the first form of any essence its first matter, since our five senses present only forms; even atoms isolated by chemistry are known through ways of receiving and being received, i.e. as forces, not matter; all the more in upper worlds where nothing sensed or imagined applies."@en ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: צורה ראשונה (tzurah rishonah); חומר ראשון."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 10, para 2 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .

pmc:KabbalahAshlagEinHasagaBaMahut a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "The senses grasp only forms, never matter"@en, "Die Sinne erfassen nur Formen, nie Materie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Epistemic limit stated as a warning: no attainment of matter or essence is possible through the five senses, only of forms of accidents arising in cooperation with the senses."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:KabbalahAshlagTzuraRishonaHomer ;
    skos:note "Hebrew term in the text: השגה במהות (hasagah ba-mahut)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Kabbalah ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:HaqdamaLeTalmudEserHaSefirot ;
    dcterms:source "Ashlag, Talmud Eser ha-Sefirot, Part 1, Histaklut Penimit, ch. 10, para 2 (Sefaria segmentation), Hebrew text of the Sefaria library, version Jerusalem, 1956-1966 (edition from Sefaria's version record; no title page in the text layer)" .
